n></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-in work"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">wiringcliff</span><span class="ttl">check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s EXEMPT table expires as a block and the checker then hard-fails -- and NOT ONE of the entries is a cheap wiring: every reason string names a prerequisite that does not exist.  DERIVE the population and the date, never quote them: `grep -n 2026-09-20 tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py&#x27; for the set (the file states the count in its own comment), and the comparison is `d &lt; today&#x27; so the block is still VALID on its stamped date and first reds the day after.  (SUPERSEDED TITLE, kept only as the demoted record of what was claimed: &quot;EIGHT probe-wiring exemptions expire on 2026-09-20 together and the checker hard-fails -- four are cheap, only four need a design round&quot;.  Wrong on the count, wrong on the date by one in the safe direction, and wrong that any are cheap; its own halves did not add up against the population.)</span><span class="tip">check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s EXEMPT table expires as a block and the checker then hard-fails -- and NOT ONE of the entries is a cheap wiring: every reason string names a prerequisite that does not exist.  DERIVE the population and the date, never quote them: `grep -n 2026-09-20 tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py&#x27; for the set (the file states the count in its own comment), and the comparison is `d &lt; today&#x27; so the block is still VALID on its stamped date and first reds the day after.  (SUPERSEDED TITLE, kept only as the demoted record of what was claimed: &quot;EIGHT probe-wiring exemptions expire on 2026-09-20 together and the checker hard-fails -- four are cheap, only four need a design round&quot;.  Wrong on the count, wrong on the date by one in the safe direction, and wrong that any are cheap; its own halves did not add up against the population.) — commits: 8404520 eec0f4a 8d038908 8faf4a16 — witness: harness:MEASURED by running check_probe_wiring.py at --today 2026-09-19 (PASS) and --today 2026-09-21 (FAIL, 8 problems) — note: [2026-10-18, #566] regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py is wired into gate 14 (regress/gate_arm.sh, 41 checks) and its 2026-10-30 exemption deleted.  Next due: alpha_tbi_probe.py 2026-10-22 and lca_badval 10-23, lca_widewrite 10-26, lca_isalane 10-27 (the other session&#x27;s), then the four wdc_* probes 11-05 .. 12-03.  The `ip30_abort_probe&#x27; entry in the due list below is history.  ||  *** STATUS 2026-10-18 (#565): ppc_rldicl_probe.py WIRED into gate_ppc.sh (gate 13) and its exemption DELETED, five days before it would have refused every commit (dated 2026-10-22; `d &lt; today&#x27;).  Gate 13 PASS 140 checks, the rldicl block&#x27;s 30 among them (regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/gatewire_20261018/gate13/).  NEXT DUE: alpha_tbi_probe.py 2026-10-22 -- refuses from 10-23; the other session&#x27;s Alpha area, so its gate block or an owner re-date is owed; then lca_badval 10-23, lca_widewrite 10-26, lca_isalane 10-27, ip30_abort_probe 10-30 and the four wdc_* probes 11-05..12-03.  THIS ROW STAYS OPEN. ***  ||  *** STATUS 2026-09-18 (GXEMUL): #536 SHIPS -- mk48_nvram_probe.py (57 rows) and hpcmips_ctor_probe.py (28 construction IDs) wired into gate_arm.sh; the other eleven 2026-09-20 exemptions re-dated to 2026-09-27 BY OWNER RULING; the selftest&#x27;s M5a/M5b days DERIVED from the table, M5a ON the stamped date (the old literals: 21/22; a d &lt;= today mutant: 21/22).  Pass 2 + §F2, nine seats, fable5 LAST: SHIP.  THIS ROW STAYS OPEN: the eleven fall due again as ONE block on 2026-09-28 -- `exemptcliff` owns that; FILED from the round: hpcmipsc2, exemptcal, m5dayb. ***
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:4662:  -- against the wired controls in the same batch: sh_iprbcd_probe.py, sgi_re_rgb_probe.py, gdrom_default_probe.py and diff_wdc_identify.c all ARE referenced.  `run.sh` runs an explicit `GATES=(...)` list and the four appear nowhere outside `regress/` and the wiring checker itself. *** TWO OF THE FOUR ARE HIGH-SEVERITY ROWS.  Delete `| (vaddr &amp; ((1ULL &lt;&lt; pageSizeShift) - 1))` from `memory_alpha.c` and a HIGH page-walk defect is back with a CLEAN BATTERY. *** **THE SEAT EXPLICITLY DECLINED TO CLAIM THIS AS NEW, which is the right call and is why it lands here rather than as a fresh row:** `check_probe_wiring.py` already classifies all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` -- correctly, by the ladder&#x27;s witness/detector timing line -- and its own entry for `lca_confbus_probe.py` says *&quot;but this probe RUNS IN NO GATE, so the coverage exists and is never executed: wiringcliff&quot;*. *** BUT THAT CHECKER IS UNCOMMITTED, so **nothing in any committed tree reports this today.** ***  The four closures are HONEST -- their `witness:` says `probe:`, which is exactly what it is -- and what is absent is STANDING DEFENCE.  The seat&#x27;s disposition, adopted: this belongs in each round record as a DISCLOSED RESIDUAL on those four rows, not only as one filed id, because a reader of `alphapfnoffset` alone cannot see it.  *** SCOPE NOTE FROM THE FABLE ADJUDICATION, 2026-09-17: MAKE SURE THE FOUR `CLASS_WITNESS` PROBES ARE IN THIS ROW&#x27;S SCOPE, NOT ONLY THE DATED EXEMPTIONS. ***  This row&#x27;s own title is about the EXEMPT table expiring, and the four unwired witnesses (`lca_confbus_probe.py`, `lca_confwidth_probe.py`, `alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py`, `alpha_harness_probe.py`) are a different population -- classified `CLASS_WITNESS`, never exempted, simply never run. *** AND A TRAP THAT WOULD BITE THE FIX: `lca_confwidth_probe.py` MUST NOT BE WIRED AS-IS. ***  It scores **2/6 at HEAD** (measured 2026-09-17, `regress/artifacts/lcaconfwidth/head_20260917/`) because `#518` replaced the IOC_CONF kill with a decline.  Wiring it produces a PHANTOM RED; the remedy there is RE-PIN OR RETIRE, under the oracle-correction rule&#x27;s order -- re-pin first, measure the committed build red under the new expectations, then change anything. **AND THE COMMITTED TREE ALREADY KNOWS**, which sharpens the gap rather than excusing it: `check_probe_wiring.py` carries all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` with their scores.  *The gap is the FAILING, not the knowing* -- the checker deliberately does not fail on that class.  *** OWNER DECISION 2026-09-17: STAGGER -- wire the cheap ones, re-date the rest with SEPARATED deadlines and the owing round named on each.  A blanket extension was declined for the reason this checker&#x27;s own header gives: debt that expires, not debt that disappears -- and the present cliff exists because ONE deliberate alignment of two #442 debts was then copied by nine later exemptions. ***  THE ELEVEN ARE NOT ONE JOB.  Derived 2026-09-17 by reading each probe rather than its exemption text, and they fall into FIVE classes: (1) THREE ALPHA PROBES -- alpha_tbi, lca_badval, lca_isalane -- share ONE blocker; (2) FOUR wdc_* probes are TWO-LEG DIFFERENTIALS needing a single-leg mode, and two of those additionally need rig images the battery does not build; (3) fbpending_drain is REPORT-ONLY until EXPECT_CAP is designed; (4) mk48_nvram needs an mvme187 leg on gate_m88k_rounding.sh; (5) ppc_rldicl lacks the RESULT/CONTROL protocol AND is on the do-not-commit list, so it CANNOT be wired at all and must be re-dated whatever else happens.  *** THE FINDING THAT CHANGES THE PLAN, AND IT IS A WRONG PREMISE IN THE EXEMPTION&#x27;S OWN REASON.  Measured, not reasoned. ***  All three Alpha entries read &#x27;no gate runs an Alpha machine; gate_crossfamily.sh is the named home and giving it one is a harness round&#x27;.  That premise is TRUE OF RIGS AND FALSE OF PROBES.  gate_crossfamily.sh (gate 5) drives BOOTABLE RIG IMAGES through drive_guest.py, so &#x27;an Alpha leg&#x27; reads as &#x27;obtain a bootable Alpha guest&#x27;, which genuinely is a harness round.  But measured against the probes themselves: NONE of the three references a disk image at all; each execs `-E alpha&#x27; as a rung-3 COLD-DEBUGGER probe; and each already emits the parseable token a gate scores (ALPHATBI_RESULT, LCABADVAL_RESULT, LCAISALANE_RESULT).  gate_arm.sh already wires probes in exactly this shape -- `python3 &lt;probe&gt;.py &quot;$BIN&quot; &gt; &quot;$LOG&quot; 2&gt;&amp;1 || true&#x27; followed by count rows -- and runs SIX of them.  So what these three need is a PROBE SECTION, not an Alpha rig: roughly six lines apiece in an idiom the tree already uses six times.  ONE gate run discharges all three.  THE STAGGER, therefore: WIRE the three Alpha probes into gate 5 as a probe section (they also fit its stated purpose -- &#x27;non-MIPS CPU cores actually execute guest code&#x27; -- since a cold-debugger probe executing real Alpha instructions is precisely that).  RE-DATE the other eight to separated deadlines by CLASS, so the next cliff cannot re-form: the four wdc_* together behind the single-leg-mode instrument change, fbpending_drain behind EXPECT_CAP, mk48_nvram behind the mvme187 leg, ppc_rldicl on its own and longest, since it is blocked by a do-not-commit constraint rather than by work.  NOT DONE IN THIS TURN, DELIBERATELY: the exemption block states that each wiring owes ONE CLEAN GATE RUN proving it green before it ships, citing FOUR probes that shipped latently RED because the commit adding them never fired the gate.  A gate run contends with the #531 measurement in flight, so the wiring lands with its gate run and not before.  The deletion rule is already recorded here and is followed: a wired probe that KEEPS its exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it, so each entry is DELETED in the SAME edit that adds its wiring.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — RULING-REV2 — SECOND REVISION, on 7 of 9 seats (opus5 now landed; agy not fired).  THE FIRST REVISION, ONE ENTRY ABOVE, IS SUPERSEDED IN THREE PLACES AND SAYS SO HERE RATHER THAN BEING EDITED: it kept fbpending design-blocked on a cap derivation (the cap is the WRONG INSTRUMENT -- the bound is already gated by an equality); it kept four WDC files in one round (they are 3 + 1, and _sig&#x27;s media blocker is MEASURED FALSE); and it counted six obligations (there are SEVEN, and my own deriver printed the seventh at check_probe_wiring.py:1328 and I read past it -- the third correlate-not-the-property error of the day, all mine).  Every Opus claim relied on here was re-verified in the tree before this was written: gate_offline.sh:1084/:1165, check_probe_wiring.py:1328, sig_probe.py:75, gate_asan_sweep.sh:99.  DISPOSITION, REV 2.  (1) TWO rounds, not one: `wdcaltoffleg&#x27; owns the three altoffset files (one module, one rig, one media family; the parent&#x27;s `ok&#x27; first; _4bit&#x27;s single-leg form is an ORACLE CHOICE and says so; _sig owes an oracle REDESIGN, not a bolted-on contract); `wdcsingleleg&#x27; is RETITLED to addtoinbuf alone, with the poisoned image and the endianness axis as its dependencies.  (2) THREE things are decidable TODAY and all three go in the wiringcliff commit after #516: hpcmips WIRED into gate_asan_sweep.sh BEFORE the :99 gate_skip, additive rows named, its EXEMPT entry DELETED in the same edit; fbpending WIRED with NO CAP as an apparatus-rot row named for what it tests, its EXEMPT entry deleted in the same edit, and the SM_EXEMPT fbpending_bound lane discharged the same way (it is the cheapest item in the set); the checker&#x27;s FALSE comment at :1333-1334 and _sig&#x27;s FALSE reason string corrected as L4s.  (3) The three altoffset entries re-dated naming `wdcaltoffleg&#x27;; addtoinbuf re-dated naming `wdcsingleleg&#x27;; each DELETED in the same edit as its wiring when its round ships.  (4) NEW ROW `witnessclassdoor&#x27; (med): the CLASS_WITNESS field is an undated door for un-gated detectors; the fix is a class rule with a dated cutoff, like every checker change here -- its own round, not a rider.  On the record: the ledger&#x27;s EIGHT was an expired measurement (8 -&gt; 7 -&gt; 6), not a transcription; DERIVED section 9 corrects section 1. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/ — record: 2026-09-24 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #548 (2026-09-24) discharged one of the eleven 2026-09-27 exemptions: fbpending_drain_probe.py is wired into gate_arm.sh (all four timers) and its entry deleted.  TEN remain, still due together; the owner&#x27;s ruling on that cliff is pending.</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — DISSENT — MEASURING seat (Agent tool); ran two read-only emulator launches, otherwise read.  PART (2) IS THE WRONG ONE, and its fbpending half is wrong ON THE MERITS: the probe&#x27;s own header (:36-45) says the post-fix backlog is a MODULAR RESIDUE of the tick count (3 at 4 s, 100 at 46 s, 375 at 0.5 s -- not monotone in accrual), so `--expect-cap&#x27; is one-sided and cannot distinguish 762 from 7; `--learn&#x27; is a disassembly dump, not a cap-learner; and THE BOUND&#x27;S VALUE IS ALREADY GATED BY AN EQUALITY -- regress/diff_fbpending_bound.c (R5 the bound IS this timer&#x27;s rate; R6/R6b) run by gate_offline.sh:1259-1277, green.  A cap is strictly weaker than shipped coverage aimed at the same property; the header records a one-token mutant (freq/100.0) that &#x27;destroyed 99% of the guest&#x27;s clock while passing this probe&#x27; under any cap.  Right decision: NO CAP -- report-only mode already ends sys.exit(0 if ok else 1) on ELEVEN control rows, a real failable oracle for APPARATUS ROT, wirable today if named for what it tests.  hpcmips: gate_asan_sweep.sh IS the home (verified: hpcmips is not on AB_EXEMPT so the sweep already requires every subtype to construct; :539 hosts sgi_eaddr_probe.py on build/gxemul with the same shape; 55 s sweep, no wall-clock oracle; -x has precedent at gate_sh_rounding.sh:434) -- BUT the section must sit BEFORE the `gate_skip &quot;no ASan build&quot;&#x27; at :99, which EXITS the gate (silent coverage loss scored SKIP -- sgi_eaddr already inherits it), and the wiring must name its ADDITIVE rows (C3/C4 acceptance-is-a-real-lookup, S2 source order, R1&#x27;s fail-closed allowlist) because the headline is already covered by the sweep.  THE FOUR WDC FILES ARE 3 + 1: _sig and _4bit `import wdc_altoffset_probe as W&#x27;; addtoinbuf is a separate instrument with a poisoned-image, disk-content-tied, endianness-axis dependency.  *** MEASURED: _sig&#x27;s &#x27;needs a ciR: CD-ROM rig the battery does not build&#x27; is FALSE -- _images/wdc-scratch-64m.img attached `ciR:&#x27; reports &#x27;IDE CD-ROM id 0, read-only&#x27;; the c is a PREFIX. ***  _4bit&#x27;s variadic legs already accept one; its single-leg form is a NEW ORACLE choice, not a mode.  SEVEN obligations, not six: gate_offline.sh:1084 SM_EXEMPT fbpending_bound:2026-09-20, enforced at :1165 -- and it is the only genuinely cheap one.  The ledger&#x27;s EIGHT was correct when written (8 -&gt; 7 -&gt; 6, two discharges on 2026-08-30): an expired measurement, not a transcription.  AND THE POPULATION GROWS THROUGH AN UNDATED DOOR: &gt;= 8 of 18 CLASS_WITNESS entries are post-fix-green (the checker&#x27;s own definition of a detector), invisible because un-gated witnesses render `not run (correct)&#x27;; today&#x27;s lca_irqstub_probe.py note is an instance.  Three of its own derivers failed and were caught by contradictions between its own outputs -- recorded in its answer. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — REVISE — REVISE.  Part (2)&#x27;s one-run cap is wrong.  Keep ONE WDC design round with EXPLICIT FIXTURE OWNERSHIP.  &#x27;A finite re-date still expires, but naming a round does not establish a delivery plan.&#x27;  Read the four WDC files, fbpending, hpcmips and gate_asan_sweep.sh. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/codex.txt</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — NOT-FIRED — DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED (owner ruling 2026-08-30: agy is the measurement reserve); the panel had two file-reading seats and the Opus seat measured.  Recorded as a decision so it cannot read as a seat failure or as agreement.</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — DISSENT — FILE-READING, and it VERIFIED rather than reasoned -- the strongest answer of the panel.  DISSENT on the binary split and on parts (2) and (3); part (1) upheld as one round.  Three findings, each re-verified by the loop before ruling: (i) hpcmips IS CONTROLLABLE and is &#x27;the one decision this project can actually take today&#x27; -- gate_asan_sweep.sh IS the construction gate, already hosts sgi_eaddr_probe.py as a construction-time value oracle on the NORMAL binary, and hpcmips constructor deaths were already this gate&#x27;s ratchet (removed from AB_EXEMPT after #444); the probe is self-contained (--binary, HPCMIPS_CTOR_PASS/_FAIL, sys.exit(main()), no rig image).  &#x27;Calling it not a cheap wiring because the reason string still says wants is the correlate-not-the-property failure.&#x27;  (ii) fbpending is DESIGN-blocked, not one-run: `--expect-cap` is one-sided `bD &lt;= CAP` and CANNOT distinguish a bound of 762 from 7 -- the probe&#x27;s own header says so -- so one run would take N from a residue; the design step is deriving N from pending_bound/freq (dev_footbridge.c) then VALIDATING by a run.  (iii) *** THE CHECKER&#x27;S OWN LIVE COMMENT ABOVE EXEMPT IS FALSE ***: &#x27;These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and exits nonzero on failure&#x27; -- false of all four WDC files; a re-date that does not correct it leaves the tool asserting the claim this row just retired.  Q2: ONE round for the shared instrument change; splitting rig images into their own round &#x27;invents a design that is not there&#x27; -- but the images must be in the round&#x27;s OWED WORK, not merely its exemption name.  Q3: part (3) as written is debt-that-disappears for _sig and addtoinbuf; the form that expires is: when the named round ships, the exemption is DELETED in the same edit as the wiring (the pit / sh4_bsc precedent already in the checker).  fbpending and hpcmips correctly keep 2026-09-20. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/grok.txt</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — DISSENT — kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE (packet-fed; the CLI walled).  Wrong in part (1); the split leaks in two places.  (a) PREMISE 4 vs PREMISE 5 IS A REAL TENSION: altoffset&#x27;s `ok&#x27; has explicit expectations, so `sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)&#x27; is a one-line today-cheap change -- both premises hold only if &#x27;wiring&#x27; means assertable-by-gate-10 and that requires the single-leg mode.  (b) hpcmips sits on the controllable side only on an unverified gate NAME -- &#x27;iff the gate verifies&#x27;.  The loop&#x27;s error, in its words: &#x27;treating has-a-reason-string-naming-a-prerequisite as proof the prerequisite is real and indivisible -- premise 5 is direct evidence against that for altoffset, and premise 4 was ratified rather than re-derived.&#x27;  Also: sig owes an ORACLE REDESIGN, not a bolted-on contract.  [TRANSPORT NOTE: the kimi CLI walled on this panel (350-byte 403 error file); this answer came through the kimi-k3:cloud substitute, so the seat is COVERED, not lost.] — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/ollama_kimi.txt</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — DISSENT — PACKET-FED.  The split is right on its real axis (ENFORCEABILITY, premise 3) but mislabeled; part (3) is wrong as applied to two of the four WDC entries (_sig, addtoinbuf), which it re-dates naming a round that cannot deliver their images. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260909_140221/ollama_glm.txt</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — DISSENT — PACKET-FED.  Not right.  Part (2) wrong: hpcmips &#x27;infrastructure-blocked&#x27; (REASONED from the reason string -- REFUTED by grok&#x27;s verified reading and the loop&#x27;s own check of gate_asan_sweep.sh); fbpending&#x27;s cap needs a design argument (RIGHT).  Part (1): split into single-leg and rig-image rounds (