held for the Fable adjudication, which is HELD by owner directive (the same hold the peer session recorded at 10:2x on 09-19).  Nothing else blocks it.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  Confirmed from the source during #530&#x27;s pass 2 (grok, file-reading): lca_isa&#x27;s nested memory_rw(LCA_ISA_BASE + P, ...) carries no PHYSICAL flag, so 0x1d00002ff is treated as a VIRTUAL address and works only because ptbr == 0 identity-maps it (memory_alpha.c).  The row&#x27;s premise stands; nothing new is claimed.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — fable5 RULED LAST on #540 pass 1 (identity verified: claude-fable-5-1, CHECKPOINT quoted).  GO-WITH-CHANGES.  Q2: the LANE cells are FLOOR, by a binding discriminator (a body-partitioned axis whose partition reaches an operand of the edited statement or is re-tested on its output path) -- six rows owed; my two reasons were the WRONG reasons (floor is a property of the DIFF; cost is never a criterion).  Q3: HIGH.  F2 heading + F11 (&#x27;two unlatched lines&#x27; -- the second is a gated debug()) corrected; F14 refined to a THREE-WAY scorer (ESCAPED / KILLED / INVALID). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/fable5_p1.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/fable5_p1.md] — record: 2026-09-18 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  No panel was ever convened on this stage.  Two entries (grok, opus5) recorded 2026-09-18 by the unread-seat sweep, neither citing a panel dir.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1, Opus 5 (READ-ONLY this pass).  VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES.  THE SCORER TRAP: CONTROL=DEAD prints 0/0, which an ok==total scorer counts as an ESCAPE for (c) and every host-death mutant -&gt; fable5&#x27;s three-way scorer.  (e&#x27;) and (f) escape; the 21066 is EV4 (no BWX) -&gt; LDL/STL lane rows.  Found E1 (swpctx treats the PCBB as virtual -&gt; alphapcbbvirt), E2 (a PHYSICAL RAM access installs a VA==PA translation -&gt; physupdtlb), E3, E4 (alphavmkill), E5.  MED as witnessed. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/opus5_p1.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/opus5_p1.md]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1, the DEDICATED cxlaunch job (owner directive: each panel adds one).  VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES -- candidate (f), PHYSICAL only for ports &gt;= 0x200, survives all 13 rows; the cell map shows every armed len&gt;1 / ofs 1-3 cell NO ROW.  (g) (return the inner read status) NO ROW.  P2 FALSE as written (masked mapping).  P4: bus_isa also adds LPT/WDC/FDC/VGA (all DM_DEFAULT, checked).  Found the same two detector gaps as the main loop&#x27;s draft, independently. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/codex_adv540p1.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/codex_adv540p1.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1.  VERDICT: GO.  (a) 11/13, (b) 11/13, (c) CONTROL=DEAD, (d) EQUIVALENT with a full `cache&#x27; inventory, (e) 9/13.  HIGH.  Only 3 device memory_rw calls omit PHYSICAL (the two here + dev_ether.c, a guest pointer) -- matches the main loop&#x27;s complement census exactly. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/agy.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/agy.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1.  VERDICT: GO; HIGH.  Scored (c) 11/13 -- REFUTED by six seats: the pre-arm `live&#x27; row also forwards, so (c) is CONTROL=DEAD.  CACHE_NONE is 2, not 0, so bare PHYSICAL is equivalent here but not the same encoding.  Unnamed option: wrap the address in K0SEG -- passes the probe, fails in user mode. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/grok.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/grok.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1, kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE (PACKET-FED; an extra answer beside the CLI).  VERDICT: GO.  &#x27;Works ONLY&#x27; slightly strong -- a mapped VA misroutes.  (c) CONTROL=DEAD; (d) equivalent-in-effect.  Witness gaps named: no row on the outer write&#x27;s completion; post-arm rows are COM1-only. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_kimi.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_kimi.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: GO -- the fix cannot regress ptbr == 0.  Named premises: SCR R/W, address-matched miss rows (both settled by the probe).  Its (c) &#x27;uninitialised byte&#x27; is refuted by memory_rw&#x27;s #95 pre-zero.  Unnamed options (translator-side identity; latch only) rejected. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_glm.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_glm.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES -- rule out a post-swpctx outer K0SEG failure (answered: `sp lsr ans&#x27; + the address-tagged inner misses); (d) not checkable from the packet (settled by five file-reading seats). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_deepseek.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_deepseek.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #540 PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: GO; HIGH.  Its &#x27;no file previously combined CACHE_NONE|PHYSICAL&#x27; is FALSE by the census it quotes (dev_ps2_stuff.c x2).  Its r/w-miss-after-fix doubt is settled: PHYSICAL skips translation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_minimax.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/p1_20260918/panel_20260918_211907/ollama_minimax.txt]</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** CROSS-SPEC REVIEW OF ALL THREE WITNESS SPECS AS A SET -- none had been reviewed against the others, each was written in isolation.  VERDICT: DO NOT BUILD THE THUMB SPEC AS WRITTEN (&#x27;the TTB plant is a session bomb&#x27;).  BUILD ORDER: MSR first, then Alpha with one added stop, then Thumb. ***  IT CORRECTED ITS OWN EARLIER SPEC TWICE MORE.  (1) THE `printed()&#x27; INSTRUCTION WAS FALSE: it had told me to shun arm_bfx_width_probe.py because &#x27;the debugger prints r0 = 0x...&#x27;.  debugger_parse_expression returns PARSE_NUMBER, so `print &lt;reg&gt;&#x27; emits a BARE 0x... line; `reg&#x27; is the command with the prefix.  A builder who &#x27;fixed&#x27; the regex would score EVERY print as ABSENT -- and arm_flags_probe.py has NO printed() at all, so the advice was unfollowable.  Copy verbatim from lca_isalane_probe.py:397-399.  (2) THE MSR FAKE-GREEN MECHANISM WAS THE WRONG ONE: already-USR32 gives m=10 alive, which reds honestly (wrong-reason FAIL), NOT a kill-row green.  The real fake-green is encoding-nop / c-bit-off / MSR-never-stepped -&gt; still SVC32, alive -&gt; GREEN, because that IS the post-fix decline appearance.  Guarding USR32 would have guarded the path that reds.  NEW BUILD TRAP: DO NOT COPY arm_flags_probe.py&#x27;s session() wrapper -- it dumps ONCE AT THE END, and this guest calls exit(1), so the arming word must be dumped BETWEEN step 2 and the killing step.  That is also why MSR is built FIRST: it is the only one of the three that forces the mid-session dump, so Thumb inherits proven machinery.  ALPHA GAP: lcaisaphys states its stop in PROSE and emits no CONTROL=DEAD / RESULT=0/0, so a failed swpctx yields ~10/13 with defect rows GREEN that a RESULT grep will not refuse -- copy the ARM token.  ONE GUARD FOR ALL THREE: a positive un-fakeable observable that the bad path is ARMED, on the SAME PROCESS that issues the stimulus, before any defect row is read; red there is SETUP-FAILED.  Do NOT share an MMU-arming prologue between the ARM probes; share only pty/wait/send/sw()/-A.  `-T&#x27; is a silent coupler (turns a physical miss into host death); `-K&#x27; is redundant with `-V&#x27;.  All of this is in regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/SPEC_AMENDMENTS_READ_BEFORE_BUILDING.md, beside the spec rather than in this row, per the #490 lesson. — evidence: regress/artifacts/witnessspecset/CROSSREVIEW_grok_20260917.txt and CROSSREVIEW_brief_20260917.md; regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/SPEC_AMENDMENTS_READ_BEFORE_BUILDING.md</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcaisasize</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa): `relative_addr &gt;&gt;= 5` discards the a&lt;4:3&gt; TRANSFER-SIZE field, so 7 of the HRM&#x27;s 11 legal encodings are under-copied -- and on the canonical LDL path the guard never fires, making it silent and total</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa): `relative_addr &gt;&gt;= 5` discards the a&lt;4:3&gt; TRANSFER-SIZE field, so 7 of the HRM&#x27;s 11 legal encodings are under-copied -- and on the canonical LDL path the guard never fires, making it silent and total — witness: none -- filed from a pass-1 ruling.  The rung-3 fixture exists (`regress/lca_isalane_probe.py`); the attempt is owed.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** THREE REAL DEFECTS, NOT ONE -- these rows had ZERO seat entries of any kind until now. ***  REAL.  Independent of `lcaisaqword&#x27; as that row asserts, but the two SHARE ONE DECODE WORD and should land in ONE Table 6-3 decoder round -- **do not split them, and do not take qword first**.  *** THE #530 RE-TABLE CONDITION, which is the actionable constraint: only a size fix that keys on CPU `len&#x27; -- which is WRONG against the HRM, since a&lt;4:3&gt; is the transfer size and `len&#x27; is the emulator buffer width -- would force a re-table of #530&#x27;s 352 rows.  A correct ENCODING-KEYED fix would not. *** — evidence: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/grok_lcasiblings_20260917.txt and its brief; src/devices/dev_lca.c; _scratchpad/21066_66a_hrm.txt S6.2.6.1 / Table 6-3 / S6.2.8; src/cpus/memory_alpha.c</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcaisaqword</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa): for the QUADWORD encoding a&lt;6:5&gt; is NOT ad&lt;1:0&gt;, so a quadword I/O access to port P is forwarded to port P+3 -- an ADDRESSING defect, and a fix for the width defect does not imply a fix for this</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa): for the QUADWORD encoding a&lt;6:5&gt; is NOT ad&lt;1:0&gt;, so a quadword I/O access to port P is forwarded to port P+3 -- an ADDRESSING defect, and a fix for the width defect does not imply a fix for this — witness: none -- filed from a pass-1 panel finding; the rung-3 attempt is owed.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class