0, MB=40 for a stale rS re-read on WRAPPING masks (codex&#x27;s arithmetic, not built); (3) an insertion skipped only when Rc=1 survives both probes (both CONTRACTs disclose it); (4) CENSUS_SHRINK -- one run of the fixed build with a shortened census, the literal pins&#x27; unique channel; (5) R_NOGUARD -- delete rlwimi&#x27;s `sh ?` guard, predicted 28/28, load-bearing for definedness since the fix narrowed tmp (Fable).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ip30stallgreen</span><span class="ttl">ip30_abort_probe.py reads a load-stalled session as a run whose remaining accesses never happened: session() returns alive=True for a child its 12 s poll kills, holding only the transcript read before the poll -- so on V2_assigntick, xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalling with exactly one ISR announce captured leaves all 41 gate-14 checks green</span><span class="tip">ip30_abort_probe.py reads a load-stalled session as a run whose remaining accesses never happened: session() returns alive=True for a child its 12 s poll kills, holding only the transcript read before the poll -- so on V2_assigntick, xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalling with exactly one ISR announce captured leaves all 41 gate-14 checks green — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 by #566 (GPT-6 Astra and Grok 4.7, pass 2 and F2).  A stall BEFORE a session&#x27;s access leaves its `alive&#x27; and `no&#x27; rows green -- the kill rows, `acc 30 rd&#x27;, `tick 49&#x27;, the read arms&#x27; `txt&#x27; rows -- and its `yes&#x27; row red (the write-arm and bit-50 tick sessions carry one); a count row that wants ONE announce (latch 1x, latch 28wr, latch 30wr, latch tick, xbit rev, xbit rev2) reads green whenever exactly one was captured, so V2_assigntick goes all-green when xbit rev2&#x27;s session stalls with one ISR announce captured and every other session passes.  The reap after the SIGKILL is a blocking waitpid and gate_arm.sh puts no timeout on the probe.  Repair shape: a per-session completion marker every row requires -- a probe change, owing a kill table.  Disclosed in the gate block&#x27;s comment.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"