readback - 0x1234 that is a non-negative multiple of 1000 (`_d20000 &gt;= 0&#x27;), so N = 0 passes -- table 4&#x27;s V7 log shows that row green (GLM 5.3 predicted the opposite at the closure check).  (2) V8_len4 -- under DOES NOT CATCH: the guarded body never tests len, so by the pcc2widthkills bound it is a single-operand marginal; cheap -- len takes at most four values and the probe already has guest_store64/guest_load64.  (1) and (2) are COVERAGE DEBT above the floor, FILED as the floor&#x27;s own rule says; not owed before ip30abortkill&#x27;s close.  Grok 4.7 dissented at the closure check: they need no carrier and stay disclosed in the CONTRACT (grok_close531.txt).  (3) three questions #531&#x27;s CHANGELOG block filed (`Also filed:&#x27;, under RECORDED, NOT RESOLVED) and regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/PRETABLE3.out lists the first two of -- the announce string&#x27;s TRUTH (`interrupt-status rewrite not implemented&#x27; is printed by the 0x10020 and 0x10028 write arms, which keep their stores; glm and kimi), the per-INSTANCE latch axis (N = 1 per device instance, the tree ships sgi_ip30_2, every row runs against one instance; kimi), and fall-through after a non-exiting fatal() (deepseek).  #531&#x27;s F13 ruling silenced the read arms and settled none of the three; this row does not claim them repaired, and they were on no ledger row (GPT-6 Astra, the closure check).  Owed when this row&#x27;s round runs: for (1) and (2), a row each or a recorded decision not to; for (3), an explicit disposition of each.  dev_sgi_ip30.c&#x27;s stale comment counts are #561&#x27;s held places 7-10, carried by heldrecedits; the load-stall green is ip30stallgreen.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c n