#560 and #561 HELD 30 ruled corrections on 2026-10-06 that no ledger row carries: 29 src/ comments (#560&#x27;s 12, #561&#x27;s 17; each owes est/ byte-identity and build-tree propagation) and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; comment in regress/diff_ieee_store.c (:296-301) -- the bug file&#x27;s #560 and #561 sections end `Still owed&#x27;</span><span class="tip">#560 and #561 HELD 30 ruled corrections on 2026-10-06 that no ledger row carries: 29 src/ comments (#560&#x27;s 12, #561&#x27;s 17; each owes est/ byte-identity and build-tree propagation) and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; comment in regress/diff_ieee_store.c (:296-301) -- the bug file&#x27;s #560 and #561 sections end `Still owed&#x27; — witness: none — note: filed 2026-10-18 with ip30abortkill&#x27;s closure records.  The lists are OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md&#x27;s `### #560&#x27; section (HELD (20)) and `### #561&#x27; section (HELD (17): every src/ comment, each with its ruled replacement under regress/artifacts/recordfix_20261002/adjudication_20261006/EDITS_561.json key `held&#x27;); #560&#x27;s rulings are its ADJ_FINAL.md and ADJ_HREC_FINAL.md.  This row carries the 30 of those 37 that no ledger row carried: the 29 src/ comments -- #560&#x27;s 12, dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s among them (held then because the peer session&#x27;s uncommitted work sits in that file), and #561&#x27;s 17 -- and #560&#x27;s `hrec extra&#x27; (diff_ieee_store.c:296-301).  #560&#x27;s other seven held sites (hrec 2, 9, 10, 19a-c, 20) are hrecordowed&#x27;s members hbundle_regress15:F7, hbundle_tools1:F5/F6 and hdiffieeestore:F6/F7, and stay there (GPT-6 Astra, the confirm).  Four of the 29 are #561&#x27;s places 7-10, dev_sgi_ip30.c&#x27;s stale comment counts, which ip30abortkill&#x27;s closure check first proposed to move onto ip30abortresidual -- a split of one held set (Grok 4.7).  The lists are as of 2026-10-06, and #565 has since corrected hrec 2&#x27;s claim, so the round reconciles each item against HEAD before applying it.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></t