<span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — the driver hardcodes the shared log directory and the caller does not explicitly propagate LOGDIR — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/codex_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — drive_guest.py hardcodes /tmp/gxregress in drive() and ignores LOGDIR from the environment. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/agy_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — `drive_guest.py` hardcodes `/tmp/gxregress` and `lib.sh` does not export `LOGDIR` — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/grok_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — drive_guest.py:197-199 hardcodes /tmp/gxregress; LOGDIR never read; gate_hygiene grades $LOGDIR/drive_*.log — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — but honoring $LOGDIR alone is insufficient without a caller change too — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — UNKNOWN — UNKNOWN — cannot read file:line; hardcoded /tmp/gxregress is plausible but unverified. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — a configurable log path that the script silently ignores is a test-isolation bug. (packet-only resend after the mixed-brief stall; P3 resolved) — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/minimax_resend_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 + os.environ.get at :197-199, ONE carrier shared by producer and grader. Rejects argv (a SECOND carrier - writer and grader could diverge) and a call-site prefix (the census must then remember it, and forgetting is silently inert - the defect class under repair). DETECTOR TRAP NAMED: do NOT use `env LOGDIR=...`, which exports from outside and stays green with lib.sh&#x27;s export missing - that tests half the defect. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/fable5_r1_n5_n6_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — export at lib.sh:24 AND `os.environ.get(&quot;LOGDIR&quot;) or &quot;/tmp/gxregress&quot;` at :197 - MEASURED, the or-form is REQUIRED: the .get(default) form that the other eight seats proposed writes to the FILESYSTEM ROOT when LOGDIR is empty. Also measured: the driver-only fix is CONDITIONALLY inert (dead for `LOGDIR=x; ./run.sh`, live for an exported value) - worse than uniform. A GATE-5 ROW IS MEASURED VACUOUS (in the default battery LOGDIR equals the hardcoded literal); the detector must be an offline selftest with a private LOGDIR and a synthetic rig name, asserting the FILES not the driver&#x27;s LOG= line (a half-fix kept LOG= correct while the raw log escaped). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/opus_r1_research_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh and derive both driver log paths from it. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/codex_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR in lib.sh; driver reads os.environ.get with the same default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/agy_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh; the driver joins that directory for both pty logs. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/grok_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 AND os.environ.get at :197-199, proven by a fake-emulator selftest wired into gate_offline.sh (a new selftest_logdir.py, not a gate-5 row). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export at lib.sh:25 + os.environ.get at :196-199. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export LOGDIR; driver reads it with the /tmp/gxregress default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export in lib.sh; resolve both pty paths via os.environ.get. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/minimax_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — Implemented and committed as f92e5a1 with its detector. Gate 2 PASS (122 checks) including the two new rows; the detector was negative-controlled in BOTH directions - no/no FAIL on the unfixed tree before the edit, yes/yes PASS after. Awaiting the panel&#x27;s review of the actual diff. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_closure/r1_research_closure_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — CONFIRMED — CLOSED AS ALREADY-COMPLETE, and verified before closing rather than taken from the hold. Nobody proposed dropping these -- the adjudicator found them while asked what should be closed that no seat had raised, and its point stands: FINISHED WORK HAD SAT OPEN FOR FIVE DAYS.
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:18118:OPEN, and the committed witness is exactly why it can stay open honestly rather than vaguely.  NO FIX HAS SHIPPED: `sgi_re_width_witness.py` proves the defect and defends nothing.  What remains, in order:  (1) a FIX ROUND on ONE sgi_re width site -- eligible now, since the fix SHAPE is already settled by `#337`&#x27;s precedent (latched decline, `(once)` marker), so it is an application of a decided design rather than a fresh design argument;  (2) a rung-3 witness for the pcc2 half, which has NONE -- a read-only seat specified one precisely (`-e mvme187`, CODE 0x10000, r5 = 0xfff42000, one process per fatal row) and said plainly it did not run it;  (3) the class total re-derived if either half moves: 11 today (sgi_re 6 witnessed, pcc2 5 after the M88K alignment narrowing), down from the 16 this row was filed with.  **The witness being committed changes the row&#x27;s EVIDENCE, not its STATE** -- and the check that caught the ambiguity is right to insist the difference be written down: a row whose detector is in the tree is not unstarted, and a reader seeing `open` with a committed artifact deserves to know which half is done.  *** PASS 1 IS DONE AND THE DESIGN IS SETTLED.  Eight seats answered (agy quota-walled); panel dir `_scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748`.  THE IMPLEMENTER SHOULD READ THIS BEFORE THE BRIEF -- the brief has three known defects the panel repaired. ***  **1. `break` IS NOT LEGAL C AT THESE SITES, and EIGHT OF EIGHT ANSWERING SEATS SAID SO.**  The guards sit in `if`/`else if` arms, not a `switch`, so `break` exits the nearest enclosing loop or switch -- there is none.  The correct edit is an `else if` SPLICE: the decline arm ends and control falls to the common tail.  One structural token changes per site (`if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` becomes `} else if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE) {`).  *Unanimity on a defect in the brief is the premise-audit instruction working: the seats were told not to ratify, and none did.*  **2. `return 1`, NOT `return 0` -- and two seats CHECKED it rather than reasoning.**  `memory_rw.c` coerces a 0 return to -1 and the `res &lt;= 0 &amp;&amp; !no_exceptions` arm raises `mips_cpu_exception(..., EXCEPTION_DBE, ...)`.  So `return 0` is a guest-visible DATA BUS ERROR, not a decline -- a different design with its own warrant and its own row, and very likely a guest panic on IP32.  **Nobody had checked this in the entire history of the sketch rule that demands it.**  *** 3. THE COMMON TAIL IS DEAD CODE TODAY AND THIS FIX MAKES IT LIVE.  This is a BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the round record must state. ***  `odata` is never assigned anywhere in `DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re)` -- it appears exactly twice, at its declaration and at the tail -- and every read path in the function currently `exit(1)`s.  So `memory_writemax64()` at the tail is UNREACHABLE in the shipped tree.  After the fix a declined READ falls through and executes it for the first time, handing the guest a defined 0 instead of an untouched buffer.  That is the right outcome, and **the `else if` form gets it for free while an early `return 1` would not** -- which is precisely the incident the sketch rule was minted from.  **4. THE WITNESS OBLIGATION IS DISCHARGED: 26/26, ALL SIX SITES, BOTH DIRECTIONS**, controls green, sentinel present, artifacts at `regress/artifacts/widthkillclass/opus_p1_20260830/`.  Two seats had split on whether six byte-identical sites are ONE round or SIX; they converged on the operative condition -- extend the witness first -- and then one seat did it.  **Settled by measurement rather than by argument, which is this project&#x27;s rule for splits.**  With all six witnessed the joining clause is satisfied and ONE round is licensed.  *** 5. TWO L2 ESCAPES ARE ALREADY MEASURED AGAINST THE ROW SET THE BRIEF PROPOSED.  Hand these to the measuring seat as its FIRST assignment, not its ask-again. ***  **M1 -- `len != 8 &amp;&amp; writeflag == MEM_WRITE`.**  Every STORE row stays byte-identically green while ALL SIX READ SITES DIE.  The witness probes stores only, so `writeflag` is a dimension no probe value varies -- the same shape as `#496`&#x27;s high-byte escape, on a different axis.  Worse, the attribution row reads 0 because the guest then dies at the DIRECTION guard, so even a message-grep row would not attribute the death to this class.  **The missing row is one line: `lw` at each window, post-fix `exit0`** (measured `exit1` on the committed build at all six).  **M2 -- a latch-bit collision.**  Invisible to EVERY one-access-per-session row, because each session forks a fresh emulator with `d-&gt;warned` at 0.  Only a TWO-SITES-IN-ONE-SESSION row sees it.  Six single-site rounds would structurally guarantee this blind spot, which is a MEASURABLE argument against splitting.  **M3 (structural, not built) -- the witness&#x27;s attribution rows use `&quot;...&quot; in t`, a SUBSTRING-PRESENCE test.  Deleting the latch entirely passes them.**  That is `#265`&#x27;s flood which `#269` had to undo.  Rows must COUNT (`t.count(...) == 1`), not test presence.  **6. PER-SITE LATCHES, with an in-tree warrant rather than a preference.**  `dev_wdc.c`&#x27;s own comment adjudicates the discriminator: *SIX FLAGS, NOT FOUR* -- sharing is licensed only across sites MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE AT RUNTIME (`#337`&#x27;s shared flag spans two arms of one endianness branch).  The six sgi_re windows are walked in one session by any driver bringing up the RE, so they are not mutually exclusive.  A shared bit reports one window and hides five.  **7. THE FIX&#x27;S WARRANT IS STRONGER THAN &#x27;UNIMPLEMENTED&#x27;, BUT NOT AS STRONG AS THIS POINT ORIGINALLY CLAIMED -- CORRECTED IN PLACE 2026-08-30.**  It said *&#x27;the guard is load-bearing HOST memory safety&#x27;*.  **MEASURED FALSE by `offsetof`:** the over-run lands INSIDE the same allocation (`re_linear_a[32]` IS `re_linear_b[0]`; `re_linear_b[32]` IS `de_reg[0]`), so it is UB plus SILENT INTRA-STRUCT CROSS-ARRAY CORRUPTION -- not a wild write, not a host crash, and **invisible to plain ASAN**.  The phrase survived here after being corrected in `sgilinearoob`, in the very row whose first line tells the implementer to read it before the brief: *corrected in one place, alive in one more*, which is mechanical rule 2&#x27;s exact scenario.  **AND THIS POINT BUNDLED A SECOND, SEPARATELY-UNVERIFIED CLAIM:** the `len == 1` over-read of `data[hwi+1]` is of the CALLER&#x27;S buffer, and nobody has established that buffer&#x27;s size -- so it is not &#x27;host memory safety&#x27; either.  The honest warrant is **cross-array corruption plus an unverified caller-buffer over-read**, which still settles DECLINE against IMPLEMENT and settles it for reasons that are true.  **8. NAME `sgidewidth` IN THE PRETABLE AND ROUND RECORD.**  It is a SEVENTH live width kill in the same file, deliberately excluded (different handler, different accept set, readable registers).  A round called widthkillclass that fixes 6 of 7 and does not say so writes false unanimity.</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — Ruled the scope question and then made it moot: ONE round of six, CONDITIONAL on extending the witness to all six pre-fix -- &#x27;one witnessed site does NOT license the class&#x27;.  Found the SEVENTH live width kill (`sgi_de`, one `sb` away) that the scope question was hiding, and the `sgi_mte` mis-service plus its resurrection trap.  Verified the per-site-latch question against `dev_wdc.c`&#x27;s recorded SIX-FLAGS adjudication rather than asserting the idiom.  Named the `len == 1` over-read of `data[hwi+1]` as the reason DECLINE beats IMPLEMENT.  Specified the detector in advance -- channels live and dead, the two smallest breaking edits with the row that stays green for each -- which is the obligation this seat has now discharged three rounds running. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — MEASURED, not argued, and it settled the round&#x27;s open question.  Cloned to /tmp/gxopus_497 (deliberately NOT build/, which it found mid-propagation -- dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c newer than build/gxemul -- and refused to read a tree someone else was mutating).  Applied the candidate fix at all six sites with ONE parameterised pattern asserting count==1 at each, which is itself the evidence that the six are one class.  exit(1) count 21 -&gt; 15, MAKE_RC=0, [binary -nt source] checked on every build.  DISCHARGED THE WITNESS OBLIGATION: 26/26 across all six sites and both directions.  Then measured M1 and M2 escaping the brief&#x27;s proposed row set, and named the substring-presence flood hole as a third.  Found the dead-tail behaviour change, the re_linear OOB-by-one, the TEX index defect, and that my census&#x27;s 21 was the FILE total against the handler&#x27;s 13.  Also reported the backslash trap recurring on its own apply script -- zero of six matches -- caught by running `grep | cat -A` on the WRITTEN file rather than re-reading its own source. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 1.9 MB.  Ruled SIX rounds against fable5&#x27;s one, on the ground that same-device/class/detector is a NECESSARY condition for joining and not a class-level waiver of the witness obligation -- the disagreement that opus5 then settled by discharging it.  Derived the `d-&gt;warned |= X` -&gt; `= X` mutant, which isolated per-site rows cannot see and only a cross-site retention row catches.  Independently reached the EXCEPTION_DBE result for `return 0`, and corrected my historical-tail premise: this fork pre-zeroes `data` before dispatch, so an early return yields zero rather than uninitialised bytes -- the `else if` form is still correct, for the marshalling contract rather than for stale bytes.  Found the CRIME_RE_TEX index defect under the standing licence. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — *** SEAT FAILURE -- QUOTA WALL, not agreement. ***  `Error: Individual quota reached ... Resets in 1h22m`, 109 bytes on stderr.  Recorded by name.  The wall is its FIRST on record and arrived after roughly six substantial invocations in forty minutes. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — Engaged the control-flow legality and the else-if restructure. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — 30 mentions of the break question; engaged the restructure at length. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — PACKET-FED and it found two brief defects from the inlined text alone: the census arithmetic does not reconcile as written, and §7.2&#x27;s &#x27;the model cannot serve at all&#x27; is FALSE for four of the six sites BY THE PACKET&#x27;S OWN CODE -- the store loop generalises to len 2/4/6.  That refutation is what forced the real warrant (the OOB) to be found. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — Engaged the control-flow question; concise, no thinking burn. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — MANUAL — Named the `break` defect precisely -- &#x27;exits the nearest for/while/switch, not the enclosing if&#x27; -- and predicted the failure mode a copy-paste implementer would hit at runtime.  Its latch objection (per-site deviates from the house idiom) is the one seat reading that went the other way, and it is packet-fed so it could not check `dev_wdc.c`; fable5 opened that file and the SIX-FLAGS comment settles it against this seat. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_180748</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td clas