hile collapsing a seven-seat hold to one, and established that the REAL detector is `--check`, not the controls.  Named two EQUIVALENT mutants (the non-greedy `?`; the seat filter, dead at every call site).  *** AND IT CORRECTED ME IN MY FAVOUR: my Q3(b) premise was false -- a correct discriminator never cleared wdccdbmidxfer, so I overrode nothing; the `&gt;=` slack did. One root cause, two symptoms. ***  One of its own claims did NOT reproduce (the ledgerstatelies prose phantom -- a backtick follows the colon, so no class matches it), recorded in controls.out because a seat&#x27;s finding gets checked too. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_224559</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 1.5 MB.  Its sharpest contribution is a LIMIT on the round&#x27;s own best statistic: even perfect prediction agreement &#x27;cannot validate mutant COMPLETENESS&#x27; -- it establishes only that the author understood the mutants he selected.  Names four shapes it predicts as full escapes and which sit outside the hypothesis set entirely: the write-only DBE, a repeat-access kill, a post-debug legal kill, and the LINEAR endpoint hole. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_214531</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 11 KB.  *** FIRED IN BREACH OF THE OWNER&#x27;S RESERVATION RULING, which panel.sh did not yet implement -- that gap is filed as `agyreservation` and fixed in the same commit as this entry. ***  Asked for `sb` (len=1) and `sh` (len=2) probe vectors so a NARROWING edit (e.g. `len == 4`) cannot escape -- a real coverage point about the accept side. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_214531</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 15 KB, having been at 568 bytes and looking exactly like a stall when first sampled -- the carrier&#x27;s own short-answer warning, confirmed again.  Ratified the splice (&#x27;`return 0` is a guest DBE; `break` is not legal here&#x27;), the per-site bits against the not-mutually-exclusive warrant, and the `warned`-after-`mte_reg` layout the LINEAR comments assert.  Flagged the catch-all&#x27;s queue id independently of kimi. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_214531</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 98 KB on a 36 KB brief -- the argv-cap fix working on the exact case that killed this seat earlier.  Six required changes, all records: the catch-all&#x27;s queue id in the SHIPPED COMMENT (independently found by grok), premise 4&#x27;s count, labelling `d_lessthan` as the intentional equivalence probe wherever table 2 is quoted, and citing the six-site `read_probe.out` for the 26/26 rather than the single-site artifact. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_214531</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED, and it found two brief defects from the packet alone: §C0&#x27;s tooling grep is a NULL PATTERN, and premise 1 is a pre-diff census mislabelled as current state.  Both verified and corrected.  *It also noted the null pattern was the SECOND defective output in a box whose own text confessed