ass="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgidewidth</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s sgi_de handler is a SEVENTH live width kill -- one guest `sb` to the DE window ends the host, and widthkillclass would have shipped 6 of 7</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s sgi_de handler is a SEVENTH live width kill -- one guest `sb` to the DE window ends the host, and widthkillclass would have shipped 6 of 7 — commits: 387b980 cb28a6f — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/sgidewidth/opus_witness_20260831 -- RUNG 3 on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`, cold debugger, real single-stepped instructions through real decode and real `memory_rw`, no `device_add`.  Device located at KSEG1 0xffffffffb5002000 by reading `machine_sgi.c` and the `memory_device_register` call rather than taking it from the brief; every encoding re-checked against the debugger&#x27;s own `unassemble` at run time.  LIVENESS: `sw 0xdeadbeef` then `lw` round-trips.  DEVICE-SIGNATURE: a store to `CRIME_DE_SCISSOR` echoes our own value back in the device&#x27;s own diagnostic, which RAM cannot emit.  KILL: `sb`, `sh`, `lbu`, `lhu` each give exactly one `len = N not implemented` and exit(1) -- 4/4.</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — *** REFUTED MY SEVERITY ESCALATION AND WAS RIGHT. ***  Derived that MIPS raises ADEL/ADES before `memory_rw`, so a width-w access arrives w-ALIGNED; on a page-aligned page-length window the boundary truncation can then never fire, and the declined set is 6144 / 3072 rather than my 8201 / 4105.  Widths 3/5/6/7 are unreachable and the row&#x27;s ORIGINAL &quot;one guest sb&quot; was right before I strengthened it.  Also confirmed the claim I asked it to check -- sgi_mte&#x27;s guard is dead, sgi_de&#x27;s is reachable -- and gave the fix shape: NOT #497&#x27;s splice, because this tail calls draw_primitive; an early return AFTER answering the read explicitly, which is the one place an early return is correct.  Its one contestable claim (a survival oracle cannot see a spurious draw) is resolved by kimi&#x27;s conditioning. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — (HELD-AWAITING-SEAT/defanged: opus5 -- DISCHARGED 2026-08-31)  It answered TWICE: pass 1 built the rung-3 witness and the nine-build table that chose the fix shape, and pass 2 re-measured the SHIPPED detector and found two 25/25 escapes plus a vacuous row.  (HELD-AWAITING-SEAT/defanged: opus5]  Still measuring when this landed -- running a kill table from a FROZEN copy, obeying the rule.  **A hold, not a seat failure and not agreement.**  It is held for the rung-3 witness ATTEMPT, and for one question no reading seat can settle: whether the freshly-repaired gxp  *** THE DEFANG ITSELF RE-ARMED THE MARKER THE FIRST TIME: the discharge note appended the ORIGINAL text, which still carried the live literal, so three tools kept reading the stage as held.  Fourth instance of the quoted-marker class this session, and the first committed WHILE DEFANGING. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — 1.9 MB.  Refuted the width escalation INDEPENDENTLY of fable5: *&quot;&#x27;Ordinary `ld` reaches 3/5/6/7&#x27; is false.  Only lengths 1 and 2 are ordinary aligned MIPS witnesses.&quot;*  Two file-reading seats reaching the same refutation by separate routes is what made me check it rather than defend it. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. ***  The seat check printed it by name and, since this session&#x27;s fix, it no longer inflates the tally or lands in the missing list. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  Third independent rejection of the 3/5/6/7 claim, and ratified the two things that matter: the `else` arm is reachable, and #497&#x27;s splice must not be copied.  Its Q1 answer matches fable5&#x27;s -- a latched decline that skips BOTH the switch and draw_primitive, then answers the read. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — *** 133 KB, AND ITS VERDICT LINE IS THE LITERAL WORDS &quot;verdict line first.&quot; -- a FORMAT MISS that `seat_verdicts.py` files as &quot;answered, no verdict line&quot; and that I nearly recorded as a non-answer. ***  Reading the body instead produced the round&#x27;s biggest find: it engaged with `draw_primitive`&#x27;s `default:` arm, which no other seat did, and observed that against a PRISTINE register file a spurious draw dies there -- so a startFlagged survival row CAN catch the naive-splice defect.  Chasing that opened `sgideprimop`, now filed HIGH: 254 of 256 guest-written drawing ops end the host, including two of the four DOCUMENTED primitive types.  *An unread review is neither a seat failure nor agreement, and this is the third instance this session where the body carried what the verdict line did not.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — *** THE STRONGEST PACKET-FED ANSWER ON RECORD HERE, AND I UNDER-CREDITED IT FOR AN HOUR. ***  From the packet alone it identified the alignment assumption, DERIVED BOTH BRANCHES, and correctly refused to settle the undecidable one: *&quot;widths 3/5/6/7 are guest-reachable only if this fork&#x27;s MIPS core does not raise AdEL/AdES first.  Under alignment enforcement the counts drop to 6144 declined / 3072 startFlag-set and the truncation chapter closes entirely -- but the sb/sh doors and the draw-hazard survive untouched, so the defect stands either way.&quot;*  **6144/3072 is the figure I computed only AFTER a file-reading seat told me.**  It also named my framing error exactly: an `ld` three bytes before the end is an `ld` at a MISALIGNED address, not an ordinary one.  *This is what the packet preamble asks for and it is why &quot;score a packet-fed agreement as zero&quot; was too blunt a rule -- glm did not agree, it CONDITIONED.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Defect real, fix = latched decline that skips the switch and draw_primitive but still performs the read response; one latch bit.  Called the enumerations correct -- the same unchecked confirmation as minimax. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Reported reconciling 8201/4105 from the truncation rule independently, without flagging alignment -- so it confirmed a premise it had no way to check.  Correctly caught the draw_primitive tail hazard.  *Recorded as a confirmation of a false premise rather than as agreement, which is the distinction the doctrine exists to draw.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_004034</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — Walked the goto against every exit path and found it CORRECT.  Predicted the len==2 escape (`len == 4 || len == 2`) at 25/25 from an enumerated walk and deliberately did NOT build it during a live panel -- the oracle-contention rule.  Scored six dispositions five right and ONE WRONG: deleting the 22-row artifact, where the house remedy is freeze-with-banner.  Refuted two contract claims against this round&#x27;s own preserved logs (the early-`return` catch, via mB 25/25; tail_acc uniqueness, via mE reddening THREE rows).  Answered the carrier question: fall-through vs skip-the-tail is the SCOPE AXIS of every member, not a seventh member, and belongs in the sketch rule -- now in BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — *** MEASURED TWO MORE 25/25 ESCAPES THAT SURVIVED THE 29-ROW VERSION, BOTH FLOOR BREACHES, BOTH ONE KEYSTROKE. ***  `bracegoto` (the goto moved inside the latch braces) re-opens the exact host death this round removes, measured exit1, for every decline after the first -- blind because EVERY row exercised the FIRST decline of a fresh session.  `bit5collide` (1&lt;&lt;6 -&gt; 1&lt;&lt;5) silences the decline outright; `sharedlatch` was a POINT TEST against a six-member set and five of six partners escaped.  Both repairs BOUNDED -- no new rows, no new sessions.  Also caught `hi_kill` VACUOUS BY CONSTRUCTION (pinned on an ACCEPTED width, measured identical on the pre-fix build, all eight round mutants and all five of its own).  Confirmed floor (a)+(b) hold: verbatim reinstatement 14/25, eleven reds -- measured because no artifact showed it.  Its frozen probe earned its keep: the repo copy was edited live under its run. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — 2.2 MB, and it was very nearly an unread review -- section G caught that it was recorded NOWHERE.  Three things no other seat said:  *** (1) `mC`&#x27;s &quot;23/25&quot; IS CONFOUNDED, and I put that number in the CHANGELOG and the commit message. ***  Its generator combined the shared bit with the `startFlag = 0` fallthrough, so its two reds were `dec_switch` AND `sharedlatch` -- two edits, one score.  **Pure bit-0 reuse against `mR` would lose only the latch row.**  The conclusion (own bit required) survives; the number does not measure what it was cited for.  (2) It reached the bit-collision hole independently: *&quot;primes only bit 0, so collisions with bits 1-5 pass all 25 rows&quot;*.  *** (3) A BETTER `tail_acc_x` THAN EITHER fable5&#x27;s OR MINE, and it changes the disposition. ***  We both concluded: keep the death pin, document the expiry.  Codex: **replace the ORACLE** -- program `DE_PRIM_LINE` with safe trivial state, do an accepted start-marked access, then assert draw ENTRY and `exit0`.  That keeps the &#x27;accepted accesses still draw&#x27; control while **removing the red-by-succeeding coupling entirely**, so `sgideprimop` can be fixed independently.  *Recorded as OWED rather than implemented: it needs a measured draw-entry channel for the LINE case, and the current rows are measured-green rather than vacuous -- so this is an improvement, not a floor breach, and it should not be written unmeasured.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — Reached the len==2 hole from the WITNESS side, independently of fable5: the witness killed on sb/sh/lbu/lhu while the detector&#x27;s survival rows used sb and lbu only, and `two_widths_2` stays green whether len==2 is accepted, killed or declined -- three machines, one row.  Also caught the tail_acc uniqueness L4 and the state=open-while-shipped L4. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  Refused to answer Q2/Q3 from a truncated packet and said so -- the honest answer.  See the brief defect below. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  *** CAUGHT MY BRIEF DEFECT: the diff truncated mid-comment at &quot;Clearing startFl&quot;, before the goto, the latch and the label. ***  It named the exact cut point rather than answering around it. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Challenged the one-latch-bit disposition and called Q3 &#x27;delete the goto&#x27; -- which is adjacent to the bracegoto escape opus5 then measured. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Named three semantic premises the brief left unstated rather than guessing at them. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_023544</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — awaiting fable5 — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]  Regress review owed on a CLOSED row.  **A hold, not a seat failure and not agreement.**  *** THE REASON IT MATTERS MORE THAN USUAL: this detector SHIPPED, and pass 2 then measured two 25/25 escapes it had missed -- one of which re-opens the exact host death the round exists to remove.  A regress reading is the last chance to ask whether the repaired 29 rows are sufficient or merely sufficient against the mutants someone thought to build. ***  It also carries an adopt-or-decline on a design a THIRD seat proposed that beat both of ours.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgireunmapped</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s unmatched-address else arm ends the host on ANY width in EITHER direction across 2080 bytes of its own registered window -- one guest `lb` at 0xb5001800 -- and NEITHER #497 nor sgirekills-as-scoped touches it</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s unmatched-address else arm ends the host on ANY width in EITHER direction across 2080 bytes of its own registered window -- one guest `lb` at 0xb5001800 -- and NEITHER #497 nor sgirekills-as-scoped touches it — commits: a115a4a a643e18 9f666a8 — witness: probe:regress/sgi_re_unmapped_probe.py -- 28 rows, gate-run by gate_arm.sh.  Test-first evidence in regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/killtable_20260831/: 18/28 on the pre-fix build and 28/28 on the fix, plus the ORDER PROOF for the re-pinned sibling probe (34/35 RED on the committed build under the new oracle, 35/35 after), all sentinel-verified and re-run by the coordinator rather than inherited. — note: #499 pass 3 (4daa506): 6 of 8 answering seats say DO NOT CLOSE.  TWO MEASURED CLEAN SWEEPS (M1 direction, M2 position) plus a RED-gate-on-GREEN-probe defect found by two seats independently.  Pass 4 closes the CLASS rather than the cells: the catch-all&#x27;s five inputs enumerated once, 36 -&gt; 48 rows, contract updated with what is deliberately NOT covered. Panel dir _scratchpad/panel_20260831_081810</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — *** THE STRONGEST ANSWER OF THE ROUND, AND IT ENLARGED THE OPTION SET FROM FOUR MEMBERS TO SIX -- BOTH NEW MEMBERS FOUND IN THE TREE, NOT REASONED. ***  (5) FAULT: `dev_unreadable.c` is a device whose whole access function is `return 0;`, and `machine_sgi.c` installs it TEN times ON THIS MACHINE so absent hardware raises DBE -- verified.  Rejected on EVIDENCE (no CRIME datasheet in _scratchpad, no evidence real CRIME faults there, and a wrong DBE is worse than a wrong 0 because it diverts control flow), not on principle.  (6) BACKED-ACCEPT: invent storage, the `mte_reg[]`/`de_reg[]` idiom in this same file; available for CLIP_IDS, rejected under the addition licence.  It also named a seventh candidate (ALIAS/mirror) and dismissed it.  **AND IT FOUND THE FILE&#x27;S OWN POLICY: the three sibling handlers -- sgi_de, sgi_mte, sgi_de_status -- ALREADY decline unmatched addresses without exit(1), and pristine upstream&#x27;s sgi_de was exit-free too, so the RE catch-all is UPSTREAM RESIDUE and this fix removes the file&#x27;s one exception to its own policy.**  That is a far stronger warrant than &#x27;it is a host kill&#x27;.  Gave TWO latch bits with a better warrant than #497&#x27;s (the house latch is per-MESSAGE-SITE and this arm has two texts), enumerated TWELVE boundary constants and twelve owed accept rows, and found a LATCH-BIT COLLISION escape (1&lt;&lt;5 colliding with LINB_LEN passes all three stated oracles).  ONE CLAIM REFUTED -- see the row note. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — (HELD-AWAITING-SEAT/defanged: opus5 -- DISCHARGED 2026-08-31)  The hold was for the rung-3 witness ATTEMPT the lifecycle ruling requires before a round may record itself unwitnessed.  **It did not merely attempt: it BUILT one, 32/32**, with liveness, device-signature, neighbour-device and negative controls, and widths enumerated rather than argued.  It also found THREE escapes, corrected a row of its own that failed for an ADEL rather than a code reason, and diagnosed a defect in the shared probe harness that made one of its rows unable to fail.  *The provisional-adjudication rule was right to hold: the design converged 8/9 and the ninth seat still changed the round -- an accept row at a window BASE cannot see a far-bound move, which no reading seat had noticed.* — evidence: regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/opus_witness_20260830</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 1.3 MB.  Independently derived the TEX geometry from the CRIME spec -- 28 entries of 64 bits -- which cross-checks my walk of the shipped code exactly and SHARPENED `sgitexindex` from &#x27;wrong shift&#x27; to &#x27;unit mismatch&#x27;.  Called Q5 a false dichotomy and put the correction best: **&#x27;six real windows&#x27; should read &#x27;six MODELED windows&#x27;** -- CLIP_IDS is a seventh real hardware window with no dispatch.  Listed the six accept-row addresses and the final aligned starts to pin upper-bound drift.  *Its supporting citation is a URL to an external spec, NOT read locally; the local header, struct comment and array arithmetic are what carry it.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. ***  The seat check printed it by name; a defect in the SUMMARY line that counted it as a non-answering seat was found and fixed in this same commit. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  Member 3, splice not return, 2080 confirmed, and reached CLIP_IDS independently: *&#x27;unmapped is not [right]; CRIME_RE_CLIP_IDS at 0x16e0 is a named 32-byte window the cascade never implements.&#x27;*  Said ONE latch bit -- the round&#x27;s only real disagreement, resolved against it by fable5&#x27;s per-message-site warrant. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  **Independently RE-WALKED all 4096 dispatched addresses against the header constants and confirmed the kill set exactly.**  Also challenged the `(once)` census the brief quoted from the carrier -- it counted 24 where the carrier said 9, AND IT WAS RIGHT; re-derived here by four methods and the carrier is corrected with its deriver inlined. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;OK&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Correctly flagged that the 2080 enumeration is *&#x27;conditional on window-constant values the packet asserts and never derives&#x27;* -- a fair premise-audit catch: I verified the constants from crmfbreg.h but did not inl