One wording correction: &#x27;at most two values per field&#x27; is false for op (ten second-reach values), and &#x27;every other predicate is uncovered&#x27; should read &#x27;no other predicate FAMILY is claimed closed&#x27;. ACCEPTED, corrected in place. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — UNKNOWN — [NOT-FIRED] *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling. NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — CONFIRMED — CLOSE. Residuals that do not block: dec regs liv still says &#x27;seven-store&#x27; (thirteen now) -- L4 corrected; masked equality on the eleven is actually killed (only nonzero value is all-ones) -- an UNDER-claim, safe; &#x27;two values per field&#x27; overclaims op. ACCEPTED. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — CONFIRMED — PASS. Wants one named measurement if a pass 17 ever runs: `rop &amp; 1&#x27;, the least-witnessed of the eleven. FILED in sgideprimopstrengthen. The two-value pinning is load-bearing only for registers and operands, verified on decline paths. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — MANUAL — Packet-fed. Claimed a conditional breach: &#x27;the dec regs session as diffed stores only TEN registers -- no MODE_DST store&#x27;. A PACKET ARTIFACT: the MODE_DST store was added in pass 14 and is unchanged context the pass-15 diff does not show; both file-reading seats verified it is present (probe:1119). Honestly conditional; refuted by the file. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — MANUAL — Packet-fed. Claimed `|| (x1 == 0)&#x27; escapes because &#x27;the count remains 1&#x27;. REFUTED BY READING THE GUARD: a bypass TRUE on the second reach makes the announce fire again, so every zero-operand two-draw session (dec regs, dec flood) reads 2 and reds. It misread how the latch works. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-03 — MANUAL — Packet-fed. NO BREACH in shapes (a)-(d) as stated; premise 5 non-checkable from the packet and if false the extra reads fall outside the covered shapes -- still no breach. Honest bound. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_121555</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — awaiting fable5 — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]  REGRESS (fable5 only): does the #500 sgideprimop detector still fail on the pre-fix build and pass on 840f3d0&#x27;s fix, and are its rows discriminating (a row per zero register, not a summed count)?  Held since the row closed without a regress entry; found by section I at the 2026-09-05 pcc2widthkills commit.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2defaultkill</span><span class="ttl">pcc2defaultkill  dev_pcc2.c: the `default:&#x27; arm exit(1)s on any unimplemented offset -- and kills READS the top-of-function memcpy has already served; SCCTXIACK (0x25) has no case, SCCRXIACK runs on reads</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">pcc2defaultkill  dev_pcc2.c: the `default:&#x27; arm exit(1)s on any unimplemented offset -- and kills READS the top-of-function memcpy has already served; SCCTXIACK (0x25) has no case, SCCRXIACK runs on reads — commits: ecc4d3b 2bb9cb4 — Closed in the main loop (claude-fable-5-1, author self-review disclosed, badge A) at ecc4d3b, 2026-09-05: the fix shipped with a 46-row detector (23 -&gt; 36 -&gt; 46 across a four-pass repair chain), four kill tables (6, 12 and 22 mutants; the pass-2 and pass-3 escapes each re-measured on the instrument they escaped), gate 14 four times (844/857/867/867 checks), a rung-3 witness 7/13 -&gt; 13/13.  The chain closed on pass 4 with zero floor breaches surviving adjudication; the remaining announce-grid cells are clause (e), written into the contract and filed as pcc2anngrid.  Seat verdicts at the closing pass: close (grok, deepseek, minimax, Fable-with-changes), not-close (codex derived; Opus and kimi measured -- both graded clause (e) on reading); the measurements settled it. — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/witness_20260905/defaultkill_witness.py (rung 3: guest st.b/ld.bu at uncased offsets, 7/13 red on the committed build, 13/13 on the fix; liveness + CHIPID + the arm&#x27;s own message channel); detector:regress/pcc2_default_probe.py (36 rows, gate 14; kill tables regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/killtable_20260905/ (6 mutants, 23-row instrument) + killtable3_20260905/ (12 mutants, 36-row instrument; the six pass-2 escapes also scored 23/23 on the pass-2 instrument)) — note: Filed on pass 2; addendum 2026-09-04 (Opus, pass 8): SCCTXIACK 0x25 has no case at all and SCCRXIACK&#x27;s body runs on reads.  The same ACCEPT shape pcc2widthkills turned on, at a different predicate.  Filed in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md (dated tail, `### pcc2defaultkill`, line 14290 as of 2026-09-04); this row added 2026-09-04 so the dashboard shows it -- the bug file had it, the ledger did not.  PROMOTED med -&gt; HIGH 2026-09-04 by the fix-review adjudication (Fable 5.1, ranked FIRST; GPT-6 Astra concurs HIGH): the unimplemented offsets are real PCC2 registers the in-tree guest driver writes -- if_ie.c:609 `pcc2_lancirq = ...&#x27; (0x2a), :612 `pcc2_lancerrirq&#x27; (0x2b), :655 `pcc2_lancerrstat&#x27; (0x28), verified by grep in _guest-src-openbsd22 -- and any access to them reaches default: exit(1).  This note first said the cheapest witness was `put b 0xfff4202a, 0&#x27; -&gt; host exit: MEASURED FALSE 2026-09-05 (put b never reaches a DM_DEFAULT arm; it survives and prints nothing) -- the witness is a GUEST st.b/ld.bu.  Option set to bring to pass 1: DECLINE + latched announce vs BACKED ACCEPT (the register array already backs every offset and the memcpy read path already serves it) vs FAULT; the READ side dies today too.  RE-BASED 2026-09-05: the Fable design seat found (main loop verified: machine_mvme88k.c:106 `unreadable&#x27; at 0xfff46000; if_ie.c:407-409 badpaddr match) that if_ie never attaches on this model, so the driver&#x27;s PCC2 writes never run; HIGH/FIRST rests on the measured rung-3 witness (guest st.b/ld.bu to IEICR -&gt; exit 1; put b does not reach the arm; 7/13 on the committed build, `regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/witness_20260905/`) and severity.  Pass-1 panel dir _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751.  PASS-1 PANEL CONVERGED (2026-09-05, panel_20260905_021751 + Opus/Fable): READ side keep the served byte with a latched &#x27;served 0x%02x&#x27; announce (it is a default, not a computed value: not member 4); WRITE side MEMBER 3, DECLINE + per-offset latched fatal() (once), NOT backed accept (the file&#x27;s own cased siblings -- SCCERR write-to-clear, the ICRs mask+reassert, the read-only PSCALECNT/SPEED/IACKs -- contradict a blanket store; the addition licence is unmet; it would add a bounded write into pcctwo_reg[] reachable at 0x3d).  The Opus seat BUILT both and measured the 13-row witness 13/13 under BOTH -- disposition-blind -- so the detector owes a read-after-write row in ONE session (measured A 0x0 vs B 0x5a, cased-sibling control 0x0/0x0).  if_ie never attaches (unreadable at 0xfff46000; ie_setupram early return at if_ie.c:561-564); ie0 IS configured in conf/M187 and conf/NFS (the brief&#x27;s conf grep was wrong).  Unresolved: whether the real PCC2 folds 0x40..0xfff (no MVME manual on disk; fork PCC2_SIZE 0x40 vs guest header 0x1000) -- AT PASS 1; RESOLVED the same night: the manual was fetched at the codex seat&#x27;s citation and VMESBCP2 Table 6-1 lists $FFF42040-$FFF42FFF as &#x27;PCCchip2 Registers  Repeated&#x27; (vmesbcp2.txt:4629), so the fold is the real part&#x27;s.  Cross-round: fix pcc2c040kill BEFORE any round implements a PCC2 IACK arm (the SCCRXIACK arm runs on READS and the console driver reads it -- routine entry into the C040 path).  PASS-1 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 02:17-03:27; codex via a re-worded copy after a provider refusal; three cloud seats via one re-fire after a concurrent-panel 429).  CONVERGED: fix A (Opus, measured) -- reads keep the served byte with a latched &#x27;served 0x%02x&#x27; announce, writes DECLINED with a per-offset latched fatal() (once); no backed accept; IACKs declined; the in-word bytes disclosed as a width matter.  NEW: the alias is DOCUMENTED (Motorola VMESBCP2 Table 6-1, codex); IEERR SCLR reads as zero (a store would fabricate status).  Implementation drafted (fix_pcc2_default.py + a 23-row detector reusing the width probe&#x27;s session()); ships after the width chain&#x27;s pass-13 commit.  PASS-2 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 05:56-06:2x; kimi via one re-fire with the packet inline after the pointer form stalled; glm/deepseek via 2 KB mini packets after thinking burns).  VERDICTS: NOT CLOSE (codex, grok, Opus -- Opus MEASURED two 23/23 clean sweeps), GO-WITH-CHANGES provisional (Fable), PASS (kimi, glm, deepseek, minimax).  Count the arguments: six clause-(d)-shaped escapes of the 23-row detector -&gt; L1 class-closure repair in ONE diff (13 rows, 36; data[0] + width in the announces); table 3 = 12 mutants all killed, the six pass-2 ones 23/23 on the pass-2 instrument.  Pass 3 owed on the repair diff.  PASS-3 PANEL (panel_20260905_081718) on the repair diff: close (grok, deepseek, minimax), GO-WITH-CHANGES (Fable), NO-GO (codex: three derived escapes), NOT CLOSE (Opus: SIX MEASURED clean sweeps of the 36-row instrument, one the mirror of its own pass-2 M_O1 -- the #499 shape inside the repair); kimi derived two residuals and exited without a verdict line; glm SEAT FAILURE (thinking burn x2).  Class closure #2 in one diff (fix_pcc2_501c.py): ten rows appended to existing sessions (46), the write-announce value, the latched-path read response, a len-2 read/write, the width label at len 1, one count + one read-back per offset class; M_RELOAD disclosed as unrowable.  Table 4 = 22 mutants, the ten pass-3 ones also scored on the 36-row instrument.  L4s corrected in place: &#x27;875 checks&#x27; -&gt; the gate&#x27;s own 857; &#x27;23 rows&#x27; -&gt; 46 with history; four pass-1 sentences corrected in their own place; the latch-sameoff-3 miss recorded; the tick reason narrowed (COUNT words, while running; signal-driven per timer.c:284 -- Fable&#x27;s &#x27;between instructions&#x27; premise refuted by reading) with the end-span reason added; len 8 disclosed.  Pass 4 owed on the pass-3 repair diff.  PASS-4 PANEL (panel_20260905_112529) on the pass-3 repair diff: CLOSE (grok, deepseek, minimax; Fable GO-WITH-CHANGES); NOT CLOSE (codex derived, Opus MEASURED four 46/46 sweeps and graded them clause (e) itself, kimi MEASURED the len-2 write-announce sweep and graded it (d)); glm DO-NOT-CLOSE-YET on two width-text mirror cells.  All contested cells are len- or offset-scoped and neither operand is body-tested -&gt; clause (e), disclosed with row specs, filed pcc2anngrid.  Zero floor breaches surviving adjudication; the chain CLOSES on this pass.  Records-only corrections applied: the pass-3 write-value repair re-graded L2 (Fable: &#x27;uncommitted -&gt; L1&#x27; is the provenance exemption the repair-chain ruling rejects); the two mirror cells added to the exclusions; the contract&#x27;s &#x27;44/44&#x27; (a run that never existed) -&gt; 36/36 + 46/46; the stale announce-count sentence reworded.  #501 SHIPPED 2026-09-05: reads keep the served byte (announced as served, with the width), writes declined, per-offset uint64 latch; witness 7/13 -&gt; 13/13.  PASS 2 (panel_20260905_055656) found the 23-row detector BELOW THE FLOOR six ways -- Opus MEASURED two clean sweeps (announce value -&gt; 0; member 6 on the latched path), grok/codex/Fable predicted four -- and codex found the read announce reloading the array after the copy (the tick rewrites counter interiors).  Repaired in ONE diff (L1): data[0] + `(len %d)&#x27; in the announces, 13 rows (36), all 43 offsets driven both ways; table 3 = 12 mutants, the six pass-2 ones also measured on the pass-2 instrument.  Pass 3 panel_20260905_112529.  Filed from the round: pcc2iackmodel, pcc2latchinst.</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-05 — MANUAL — The adjudicator&#x27;s hat (Agent).  SHIP: READ member 4-as-served (keep the byte, latched read announce -- gdrom announces reads too), WRITE member 3 (decline + latched announce), NOT member 6 -- the backed-accept warrant is hollow: the cited driver does not run here, and its uses are ICLR/SCLR acknowledge bits a store would retain.  FOUND FIRST (verified by the main loop: machine_mvme88k.c:106, if_ie.c:407-409): if_ie never attaches on this model, so the &#x27;in-tree driver writes these offsets&#x27; warrant behind the HIGH/FIRST ranking is a source reading contradicted by the machine description -- re-base on the rung-3 witness + severity (done).  Uniform disposition, no offset-range predicate; disclose the in-word bytes (a width matter, pcc2widecompose) and the IACKs (decline; file ack-modelling on the SCCRXIACK shape).  12 detector rows incl. R3 (write V, read back 0) pinning DECLINE vs BACKED and R10 per-offset announce count; announce shape: a per-offset bitmap, not the 32-bit width word.  Also: SCCRXIACK runs on WRITES too (no writeflag guard) -- pre-existing quirk. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — MEASURING seat (Agent).  Built BOTH candidate fixes in a scratch clone (cmp-clean vs SEC before mutant 1, .MUTANT sentinel, restored from SEC + rebuilt, both parts verified): baseline 7/13 (reproduces the committed witness), fix A (decline + per-offset latched fatal) 13/13, fix B (backed accept) 13/13 -- THE WITNESS IS DISPOSITION-BLIND (its read row has no preceding store).  Discriminator rows measured: st.b 0x5a then ld.bu at IEICR in one session reads 0x0 under A, 0x5a under B; same at IEERR; the CASED write-to-clear sibling SCCERR reads 0x0 under both (the control).  Premise 5 wrong in both directions: ie0 IS configured (conf/M187:99, conf/NFS:100 -- the brief&#x27;s conf grep was wrong) and the model BLOCKS it twice (unreadable at 0xfff46000 -&gt; iematch badpaddr fails; ie_setupram early return at if_ie.c:561-564 before the PCC2 store at :609).  L4: OUTSTANDING_BUGS&#x27;s &#x27;cheapest witness: put b&#x27; is MEASURED FALSE (put b never reaches the arm).  NEW for c040kill: SCCRXIACK&#x27;s arm has no writeflag test, so a guest LOAD of 0x27 enters reassert_interrupts(), and cl.c:1051/1234 (the console driver) reads that offset -- routine entry into the C040 path.  Warrants against member 6: the cased siblings&#x27; semantics (SCCERR clears on write; the ICRs mask + reassert; PSCALECNT/SPEED/IACKs read-only), the addition licence unmet, a bounded write into pcctwo_reg[] reachable at 0x3d.  Read side: &#x27;ACCEPT&#x27; would be a wrong record -- the served byte is a default, announce it as served.  PCC2_SIZE name collision: fork 0x40 vs the guest header 0x1000; the real fold unresolved (no MVME manual on disk at the time).  IACK offsets: do not backed-accept; modelling them opens two entries into the C040 kill -&gt; c040kill first.  Candidate diff A supplied (adopted). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING (GPT-6 Astra, max).  FIRST FIRING REFUSED by the provider&#x27;s content filter on the brief&#x27;s &#x27;kill&#x27; vocabulary (kept as codex.refused.txt); RE-FIRED ONCE with a re-worded copy (brief_defaultexit_p1.codex.md: &#x27;kill&#x27; -&gt; &#x27;exit&#x27;, facts unchanged) -- answered 14.6 KB after a web-search reconnect storm.  VERDICT: remove the exit, preserve prepared reads, member 3 for writes.  NEW FACTS: (1) the real aliasing IS documented -- Motorola VMESBCP2 Table 6-1 lists $FFF42040-$FFF42FFF as repeated PCCchip2 registers (m88k.com/Docs/172/vmesbcp2.pdf p.106) -&gt; premise 1 upgraded from &#x27;unknown&#x27; to a documented warrant (manual fetched into _scratchpad by the main loop to verify); (2) IEERR&#x27;s SCLR and the Ethernet ICLR bits are clearing operations that read as zero (manual 6-36..6-38) -&gt; a store would manufacture writable status; (3) the witness&#x27;s combined IEBERR/IEERR row does not measure IEERR independently (the exiting build dies at IEBERR first) -- IEERR&#x27;s kill follows from source; (4) two fresh session()s cannot establish per-instance latch scope (each is a new process); (5) `return 0&#x27; denotes a FAILED TRANSACTION, not inherently unmapped hardware (an IACK cycle with no interrupt pending times out on the real part) -- corrects the option set&#x27;s member-5 wording; (6) 21 cases / 43 defaults = 18 named + 12 timer-interior + 13 unnamed, independently derived; (7) `(once)&#x27; census 27 after comment removal.  Its sketch differs from Opus&#x27;s: ONE latch for the default site (writes only, reads keep the existing debug); the main loop adopts Opus&#x27;s per-offset both-direction form and records this as the alternative.  Guest reachability: none of the three cited accesses precedes the driver&#x27;s probe failures (iematch badpaddr; ie_setupram return; IEERR&#x27;s store is in iefailintr). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;N/A&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-05 — UNKNOWN — Reserved for measurement (owner ruling 2026