tools\pipeline\matrix.html:19665:*** CLOSED 2026-09-19: #530&#x27;s pass-2 repair chain closes on #538 -- its width row now rows all four byte lanes (fable5&#x27;s §F2 floor), killed the lane-1 covering escape, and reproduced on the final instrument.  Commits: 8bd97e4 (#530) + #538 (filled by the next commit). ***</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  *** THE OWED PASS IS DONE AND #530 SHIPS WITH IT -- CLOSURE, WITH THE SHA, FOLLOWS IN THE NEXT RECORDS COMMIT. ***  CLOSE6_VERDICT.md pre-committed, before any leg ran: *escapes AND len &gt; 8 is guest-reachable -&gt; L2, add a len &gt; 8 row in-round.*  Both halves established: `KILLLEN8` and `&amp;&amp; len &lt;= 8` each sweep this probe&#x27;s 352 rows (352/352), and `store_buf` (memory.c:837-857) via PROM GETENV (cpu_alpha_palcode.c:141-144) delivers len 16/64/256/1024 with a guest-controlled destination and length.  The row is `regress/lca_widewrite_probe.py`: base 3/3, both mutants 2/3, every value predicted in PRETABLE.out at 14:59:49 before any run, and the SHIPPED file re-run as shipped with the same scores.  Shipped as its own file so this probe&#x27;s 352 measured rows do not move; its header now says where the width cell is covered.  **With this commit `dev_lca.c` carries NO live host kill** -- measured with a comment-stripping parser: HEAD has exactly one, the `exit(1)` this fix removes.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">y</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;y&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-08 — ANSWERED — Censused the idiom across five files, bounded every severity, found the obvious one-character fix makes things WORSE, and identified a double-count with lcabadval. — evidence: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/codex_assess_20260908.txt</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">?</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — fable5 FIRST-HAND RE-RULING of R5 (claude-fable-5-1; checked from the transcript).  RIGHT -- the len == 0 half is DISCHARGED, no row owed -- but it is an UNREACHABLE FLOOR-SHAPED cell, not &#x27;not floor&#x27;: `len == 0&#x27; is a body-induced partition feeding `% len&#x27; -&gt; `data[ofs]&#x27;; it owes no row only because no producer issues a 0-byte access (store_buf&#x27;s chunks run 1024..1, READ; CPU accesses are 1/2/4/8 bytes, INFERRED).  M1_lenzero undetected 352/352 is what an unreachable cell predicts.  Residual, INFERRED: other memory_rw callers (debugger, DMA) were not enumerated. — evidence: _scratchpad/refable_530_538/fable5_rulings_own.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/refable_20260919/fable5_rulings_own.md] — record: 2026-09-18 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-19: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 00:24:32Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8 (a `thinking_drop&#x27; attachment), keeping this seat&#x27;s identity line.  &quot;identity verified&quot; was a SELF-REPORT, a check that cannot fail.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the first-hand fable5 ruling is the fable5 research 2026-09-19 entry below. ***  fable5 R5 ANSWERS THE HELD RESEARCH QUESTION: the len==0 DROP half DISCHARGES now -- M1_lenzero scored 352/352, EQUIVALENT by no producer (store_buf bottoms out at 1 byte; a CPU access is &gt;= 1 byte); the guard stays as a defensive `% 0` guard, no row owed, disclosed with that warrant.  The width half is not separately dischargeable: it IS the D1 floor obligation and closes with #538&#x27;s diff and its pass 2.</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-10</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-10&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-10 — WITNESS-BUILT-RED-3/16 — Agent-tool MEASURING seat, fired ~03:4x as the post-reset liveness test WITH real work (token returned: the 03:00 America/Chicago reset restored the seat).  Two-part clearance RUN (cmp CLEAN, build/gxemul 00:19:30 newer than its dev_lca.c 00:19:24, no sentinel); nothing built; build/, est/, build-asan/ verified untouched.  Built regress/lca_isalane_probe.py (alphabook1, byte loads/stores through the LCA ISA window): LCAISALANE_RESULT=13/16, four runs row-identical, ~57 s each, no retry needed under the concurrent kill table.  THREE RED ROWS, all the defect: `ofs1 zero&#x27; got 0x0 want 0x60 -- NO diagnostic, the handler returned 1 and overwrote the guest register with zero (a FALSE SUCCESS, pinned by `ofs1 devsig&#x27; (0x60 through the flat mapping), `ofs1 wide&#x27; (the same sparse address at len 4 reads 0x6000, the byte in lane 1) and `ofs1 answer&#x27; (the 0x0bad1dea pre-seed is gone: completed, not faulted)); `ofs2 exit&#x27; and `ofs3 exit&#x27; dead with `[ ofs=2 len=1 in lca_isa access function. aborting ]&#x27; / ofs=3 -- both attrib rows green.  LANE MAPPING VERIFIED: `relative_addr &gt;&gt;= 5&#x27; precedes `ofs = relative_addr &amp; 3&#x27; and the forward goes to LCA_ISA_BASE + relative_addr, so ofs == port &amp; 3 -- the lane is a FUNCTION of the port, and the defect partitions the whole 64 K ISA port space by port &amp; 3: on the console UART 0x3f8/0x3fc are fine, 0x3f9/0x3fd (IER, LSR) answer ZERO, 0x3fa/0x3fb/0x3fe/0x3ff (IIR, LCR, MSR, scratch) END THE PROCESS on a byte access.  The brief&#x27;s `same port at ofs 1&#x27; row could not be built (the lane is not an independent field) and was reformulated onto what the code does.  DISCLOSED: the WRITE direction is unrowed (the guard dominates both; one cheap session for the fix round); the uninitialised-byte path needs -T (halt_on_nonexistant_memaccess) and was NOT measured; len 4/8 are clean w.r.t. THIS defect only (one byte forwarded whatever len is); the %i-vs-size_t mismatch printed correctly here, so the attrib row keys on `in lca_isa access function&#x27; (unique in src/); driver v1 appended metadata AFTER the sentinel -- a completion-sentinel defect, fixed (RUNMETA_*.txt), both v1 runs preserved.  Frozen copy witness_20260910/lca_isalane_probe.asrun.py cmp-identical to the shipped probe. — evidence: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/witness_20260910/HEAD_run1.out</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **DO NOT CLOSE YET.**  Accepts that table 7&#x27;s zero over 15 mutants is verified and then names two things the zero does not cover: an OMITTED WIDTH CLASS, and an `expected -- not measured -- 352/352 mutant`.  Its candidate is concrete and buildable: qualify the write arm as `writeflag == MEM_WRITE &amp;&amp; len &lt;= 8`, which it EXPECTS to score 352/352 because the probe only uses widths 1/2/4/8 and their split fragments.  *** THE WIDTH AXIS IS `#499`&#x27;s OWN CLASS ARRIVING AGAIN. ***  Separately it finds SEVEN component prediction misses across six failing legs and enumerates `Wdrop` exactly as `352 - (49 + 32 + 8 + 1) = 262`, and it refutes a probe COMMENT that claims a phantom read pops the reply -- `dev_pckbc.c` shows the reply pops at `0x60` while the read is at `0x64`, so the comment is a defective coverage promise (the row assertions themselves are sound). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/codex.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **GO -- VALID CLOSING PASS.**  The lone ratifier, and the round closed on it.  Reports the diff delivered whole (1 hunk, +17/-7), all 18 legs carrying `LCAISALANE_DONE`, base 352/352, and zero escapes across 15 mutants spanning `{write, read} x {DROP, SWAP, DUPLICATE, ADD-OTHER}`.  *** Its own figures are not disputed by the dissenters; what is disputed is whether that eight-cell product COVERS the new `len == 0` guard at all. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/agy.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** SETTLES D5.  FABLE&#x27;S len-16 LANE DERIVATION IS WRONG; THE OWED THING IS STILL A ROW, NOT A PRODUCT CHANGE. ***  The L2 stands (the mutant still scores 352/352); what fails is the inference from that escape to &#x27;one-byte-of-16 is a lost byte, so the fix is wrong&#x27;.  *** THE DISCRIMINATOR: Fable&#x27;s claim is about SPARSE I/O, not sparse MEMORY, and the memory-space rows of Table 6-3 do not govern it. ***  Three independent refutations, none needing a run:  (1) THE IOC DOES NOT SIZE A CYCLE FROM memory_rw&#x27;s len.  CPU a&lt;4:3&gt; IS the transfer size and a&lt;6:3&gt; generate c_be_l&lt;3:0&gt;; the widest CPU-initiated sparse/I/O transfer in the table is QUADWORD = a PCI burst of two longwords = 8 BYTES.  **There is no 16-byte row.**  So `len&#x27; is the emulator BUFFER width and the PCI transfer size is a&lt;4:3&gt; of the ISSUE ADDRESS.  (2) EVERY store_buf GRANULE THAT CAN BE ISSUED STARTS AS BYTE.  store_buf emits psize in {1024,256,64,16,4,1} -- there is NO 8 -- and alignment then forces a&lt;4:3&gt;: a 32-aligned len-16 write has bits 4:0 zero, so a&lt;4:3&gt; = 00 = **Byte**.  Taking data[relative_addr &amp; 3] and ignoring the other fifteen is the SAME contract as STL (len 4, 3 unused) or STQ (len 8, 7 unused) to a byte-encoded address, which the model already does and the HRM requires.  **One byte is not a lost second PCI cycle: there is no second cycle, because the issue address still says Byte.**  (3) THE COUNTERFACTUAL IS NOT HARDWARE.  Split at the architectural max of 8 and run both halves through this handler&#x27;s own map: the sparse slot is 32 CPU-address bytes per port (the `&gt;&gt; 5&#x27;), a 16-aligned 16-byte write NEVER CROSSES A SLOT, so STQ at A and STQ at A+8 hit the SAME PORT, both compute the same ofs, and the second OVERWRITES the first.  Not two bytes delivered to two places.  *** AND IT NAMES THE REAL RESIDUAL, WHICH IS A DIFFERENT ROW: the comment &#x27;the size field a&lt;4:3&gt; is not decoded here&#x27; is why the model is LOSSY FOR WORD/LONG/QUAD -- the already-filed `lcaisasize&#x27; -- NOT a warrant that one byte is right for every len. ***  DISPOSITION: pin (a), one byte forwarded, **as the BYTE-ENCODING CONTRACT APPLIED TO A WIDER BUFFER -- explicitly NOT as a 16-byte PCI cycle**.  (b) product change and (c) decline-len&gt;8 are both undefensible.  *The adjudication was RIGHT to flag the clause as unestablished -- it was -- and this establishes it.  Fable did not say the call was wrong; it said it was unproven.* — evidence: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/table7_20260916/grok_lanederiv_20260917.txt and its brief; _scratchpad/21066_66a_hrm.txt S6.2.6.1 :8844-8852, Table 6-3 :8857-8884, S6.2.8 :9178-9199, :8916-8922, :8906-8907; src/core/memory.c store_buf; src/devices/dev_lca.c the ISA-lane tail</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** THE kimi CLI WALLED MID-ANSWER ON THIS PANEL AND THE EXTRACTOR SCORED IT `answered`.  Measured 2026-09-17. ***  `kimi.txt` is **2,448,106 bytes** of streamed reasoning ending, mid-plan, with: `error: failed to run prompt: provider.auth_error: 403 You&#x27;ve reached your weekly (7-day) usage limit.`  Its last words are a tool plan (*&quot;Let me grep with content mode in GXEMUL-SEC only&quot;*), not a conclusion. **THE SEAT WAS COVERED, NOT LOST**: the `kimi-k3:cloud` substitute answered on the same panel (`ollama_kimi.txt`, 8,793 b, **DO NOT CLOSE**), which is the two-transport recovery path working exactly as the seat ledger describes. *** THE REASON IT READ AS AN ANSWER IS A CONJUNCTION, AND IT CONTRADICTS THE EXTRACTOR&#x27;S OWN DOCUMENTED RULE. ***  `seat_verdicts.py` computes `is_walled = _is_wall(t[-600:], t[-4000:]) and not v`.  Measured on this file: the tail test returns **True** (the notice matches `WALL_STRONG`), and `verdict_of` returns **&#x27;PARTIAL CENSUS ONLY&#x27;** -- a verdict-shaped phrase from somewhere in the 2.4 MB stream -- so the conjunction suppresses a genuine wall.  **The file&#x27;s own comment says STRONG patterns are *&quot;a notice on their own&quot;* while WEAK ones need the extra condition; the code applies the extra condition to both.** **AUDITED RATHER THAN GENERALISED FROM ONE CASE: 2,369 seat files across 356 panel dirs; 166 carry a wall notice in the tail; TWO are hidden by the conjunction** -- this one and `panel_20260820_005715/codex.txt` (21 KB, verdict `SHIP-WITH-FIX`).  Rare, real, and one of the two is on a round still in flight. *And the audit&#x27;s FIRST answer was ZERO, because I computed the verdict from the TAIL while the shipped code computes it from the WHOLE FILE.  A known instance refuted it, which is the only reason the shortcut was caught -- the fourth time this session a check of mine keyed on a correlate of the thing rather than the thing.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/kimi.txt 2448106 b (WALLED); _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/ollama_kimi.txt 8793 b (DO NOT CLOSE)</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **NOT A VALID CLOSING PASS**, and it puts the objection as a FORMAL CONTRADICTION, which is the sharpest form any seat gave it: the comment&#x27;s premise (A) `len 0 has no producer`, P2&#x27;s (B) `no leg at 352/352`, and (C) `the 15 mutants exhaust the (d) enumeration` CANNOT ALL BE TRUE -- because if A and C hold, a guard-removal mutant is observationally identical to base, scores 352/352, and contradicts B.  It verified the hunk arithmetic exactly (17 `+`, 7 `-`, spans 15 -&gt; 25) and says the DIFF ITSELF IS SOUND; the defect is in the CLOSURE CLAIM, not the code. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/ollama_glm.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **NOT A VALID CLOSING PASS: the zero-escapes denominator omits a clean-sweep DROP mutant of the new `len == 0` guard.**  Reaches the identical contradiction independently from the packet alone.  Adds a scope point the others did not: the `len == 0` guard sits OUTSIDE both arms, so `{write, read} x {...}` -- the product as named -- may not even RANGE OVER IT. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/ollama_deepseek.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **NOT A VALID CLOSING PASS.**  Same contradiction, and it is the seat that states the DECISION PROCEDURE most usefully: DROP of the guard is a clean sweep IF `len == 0` is unreachable and a crash IF it is reachable, so `survival is exactly the question` and is LOAD-BEARING for chain closure.  Honestly flags that the reachability premise is NOT CHECKABLE FROM THE PACKET -- the packet-fed seat refusing to ratify what it cannot see. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_085545/ollama_minimax.txt</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">?</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — fable5 FIRST-HAND RE-RULING of #530 pass 2 + its adjudication pass (claude-fable-5-1 on every turn after the resume; no refusal; checked from the transcript).  A AGREE: `vc&#x27; is the one floor breach -- lane is the only body-induced axis flowing into `data[ofs]&#x27;, so the floor is {write} x {lane 0-3}; va, vb (len &gt; 16), ve (port &lt; 0x200), vg, vt1 (pre-shift bits), vt2 (stateful continuation) are clause (e), disclosed.  Both load-bearing facts re-read from the files in that turn (the handler&#x27;s selectors; #538&#x27;s per-lane red sets). — evidence: _scratchpad/refable_530_538/fable5_rulings_own.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/refable_20260919/fable5_rulings_own.md] — record: 2026-09-18 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-19: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 00:24:32Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8 (a `thinking_drop&#x27; attachment), keeping this seat&#x27;s identity line.  &quot;identity verified&quot; was a SELF-REPORT, a check that cannot fail.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the first-hand fable5 ruling is the fable5 review 2026-09-19 entry below. ***  fable5 RULED LAST on #530&#x27;s pass 2 + §F2 (identity verified: claude-fable-5-1, CHECKPOINT line quoted verbatim).  R1: L2 for vc ONLY -- lane is a floor axis because data[ofs] distinguishes all four lanes; va vb ve vg vt1 vt2 are clause-(e) debt, disclosed against the ALREADY-RULED parent classes p_port10 and lcaisasize (which the new contract must cite by name).  R2: floor closure = the four C=16 WRITE lanes {frozen L3 (shipped), l0w16 L0, low16 L1, a lane-2 cell at k=0} + an explicit store_buf chunk-list assertion; {mc2, kbc1024} is REFUTED as a closure (a lane-1 exemption escapes it); kbc1024, k=16 and the continuation cell are not floor.  R3: narrowing to escape vc = laundering; correcting the overclaiming contract = required (L4).  R4: fix the exit code AND the alive-blind retry in the closure diff.  R6: the chain closes on the first VALID pass that verifies the enumeration -- it must kill the lane-1 covering escape `&amp;&amp; (len &lt;= 8 || (P &amp; 3) != 1)` and show no lane cell open.  R7: E-DEBT correctly overturned; the filed pair was the #499 error from the other side.  -&gt; #538 is the closure round.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS -- the measuring seat, resumed with its measurement context.  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE, REVERSING ITS OWN PASS-2 READING: vc is a breach on both routes (lane is body-tested via data[ofs], crossed with the {len &gt; 8} cell pass 6 put in the floor; and vc is in-contract with no disclosure covering it).  ACROSS BOTH HEADERS the other escapes are already disclosed (va/vb by clause (iii), vg/vt1 by lcaisasize, ve by p_port10) -- only vc and vt2 were in-contract AND undisclosed.  Floor-minimal set {frozen, l0w16, low16, mc2}.  HARNESS DEFECTS in the shipped row: the retry fires on missing prints without checking `alive&#x27; (a first-session death is retried away); the width pin needs a chunk-list assertion.  Reachability runs the other way: C=16 needs no -o (BOOTED_FILE&#x27;s 15-char basename), C&gt;=64 needs a &gt;= 63-char operator string.  Ran nothing new; wrote nothing under GXEMUL-SEC. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/opus5_f2.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/opus5_f2.md]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE, mixed -- the C=16 escapes (vc ve vg vt1 vt2) breach the shipped contract, which excludes only widths 64/256/1024 in clause (iii), so narrowing cannot discharge them; va/vb and the ladder stay debt under that explicit exclusion.  F5&#x27;s remedy is the accepted disposition that is WRONG.  Closure: {l0w16, low16, mc2}, separate sessions.  NEW: mc2&#x27;s readbacks cannot tell a 32-byte request (16,16) from a 20-byte one (16,4) -- both forward s[2] and s[19] -- so the row does not pin its chunk sequence by construction.  F9 CANNOT SETTLE from its six files; (h)&#x27;s equivalence needs only the #95 pre-zero. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/codex.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/codex.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE (reversing its own pass-2 CLOSES) -- vc qualifies the write arm by a body-distinguished lvalue (P &amp; 3).  F5&#x27;s narrowing remedy &#x27;completely evades the L2 mandate&#x27;.  Closure {mc2, kbc1024} with -o padded to &gt;= 1024 characters, because GETENV clamps len to strlen+1 (a correct and load-bearing point).  TWO SIDE CLAIMS ARE WRONG: it calls the header&#x27;s `len = min(a3, strlen(s)+1)` an incorrect formula (the code is exactly that min in both branches), and says mc2 reads past the host string (the same clamp prevents it). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/agy.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/agy.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE (reversing its own pass-2 debt side, on the half it was asked to test) -- vc sweeps the row 3/3 by exempting its own lane, which the body distinguishes: the #499 / sgimtedepth4dead shape.  Closure = the four C=16 WRITE lanes + the F10 width pin; va/vb/ve/vg/vt* stay clause (e) with L4 narrowing (DEPENDS-ON does not walk into store_buf&#x27;s ladder).  KEY FINDING: {mc2, kbc1024} is a COVERING of the listed variants, not a closure -- a lane-1-only exemption `&amp;&amp; (len &lt;= 8 || (P &amp; 3) != 1)` passes both; only low16 reds it.  Also: a len&gt;8-gated write-arm fallthrough is invisible to every destination-byte row (disclose); vf is equivalent at lane 0. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/grok.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/grok.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE -- clause (e) prong (ii) plus F5-as-accepted already conclude L2; the reachability &#x27;now met&#x27; is what converts the overclaim from vacuous to BREACHED.  Closure {mc2, kbc1024} in that order.  F12 is not records: exit 0 on FAIL would neutralise the closure&#x27;s own rows -- fix it in the same diff.  Separate PROVABLE IDENTITY (vd, by algebra) from UNREACHABLE DIVERGENCE (vh).  mc2&#x27;s per-row attribution is not in the packet. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_kimi.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_kimi.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  PACKET-FED.  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE -- pass 6&#x27;s &#x27;probed set&#x27; is what shipped rows drive, every escape is outside it, and the header&#x27;s &#x27;any guard&#x27; claimed them (clause (e) L2 by itself).  va/vb ARE clause (d)&#x27;s &#x27;bound relaxed&#x27;.  Closure {mc2, kbc1024, low16} -- low16 because `len&gt;8 &amp;&amp; (P&amp;3)==1` passes the pair (independently of grok).  F5&#x27;s remedy and D1 cannot both stand.  k is body-discarded but NOT variant-discarded (vg/vt1 are caught only at k16).  vh&#x27;s equivalence is conditional on F9 (it says; codex shows the pre-zero makes it unconditional through the dispatcher). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_glm.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_glm.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  PACKET-FED.  VERDICT: L2-CLASS-CLOSURE -- F5 already establishes an in-contract undetected class; clause (e) makes that L2, and narrowing the contract after the breach is circular.  Closure {mc2, kbc1024}.  F9 CANNOT SETTLE. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_deepseek.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_deepseek.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — #530 §F2 ADJUDICATION PASS (the panel shares pass 2&#x27;s findings).  PACKET-FED.  VERDICT: OVERTURN D1 -&gt; L2-CLASS-CLOSURE -- pass 6&#x27;s &#x27;uncatchable&#x27; was a capability statement the GETENV row dissolves; va/vb are clause (d)&#x27;s own &#x27;bound relaxed&#x27;.  Closure {mc2, kbc1024}.  DISSENTS on F6/D2 (a wide-specific bug could red `wide alive` alone -- no such variant named); F8 and F14 CANNOT SETTLE from the packet. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_minimax.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/f2_8bd97e4_20260918/panel_20260918_190129/ollama_minimax.txt]</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPE -&gt; L2, FLOOR BREACH, FIX IN-ROUND. ***  The clause-(d) mutant `len == 0&#x27; -&gt; `len == 0 || len &gt; 8&#x27; scores 352/352 against the 352-row detector; base is also 352/352.  THE DISPOSITION WAS PRE-SPECIFIED BEFORE THE LEG RAN (CLOSE6_VERDICT.md:77-79): escapes AND len&gt;8 guest-reachable -&gt; L2; escapes but unreachable -&gt; clause-(e) debt.  BOTH LIMBS SATISFIED.  Reachability is VERIFIED IN SOURCE, not reasoned: memory.c:839 declares `size_t psize = 1024; /* 1024 256 64 16 4 1 */&#x27; and :843-845 issues memory_rw at psize, while cpu_alpha_palcode.c:144 is `store_buf(cpu, a2, s, len)&#x27; with a2 GUEST-SUPPLIED by PROM GETENV.  *** THE APPARATUS CONTROL THAT MAKES 352/352 A RESULT RATHER THAN A NON-EVENT: the run printed `NOTE W_len8 binary DIFFERS from base&#x27;, so the edit was LIVE IN THE OBJECT -- a mutant that never applied presents as a perfect score, identical to a clean sweep. ***  Clone controls also clean: cmp against SEC at start, and `CLONE RESTORED cmp=clean binary-nt-source=yes&#x27; at end.  WHAT IS OWED IS A ROW, NOT A PRODUCT CHANGE -- the shipped code is CORRECT at wide widths (at len 16, `(relative_addr &amp; 3) % 16&#x27; is just `relative_addr &amp; 3&#x27;, in [0,3], safely in range); it is the MUTANT that misbehaves by declining a legal wide access.  THE ROW MUST DRIVE THE NON-INSTRUCTION PATH (a PROM GETENV whose a2 lands in the ISA window), because this probe is instruction-driven and the widest Alpha store is STQ at 8 bytes -- so no instruction-driven row can EVER express len &gt; 8.  That is why the cell was empty and it is the whole difficulty.  SEPARATELY AND INDEPENDENTLY: the probe contract claimed widths `1/2/4/8 plus the 1 KB split&#x27;, omitting 16/64/256/1024 -- an L4 wrong record, corrected in the probe header the same hour. — evidence: regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/table7_20260916/KILLLEN8_RUN.out (sentinel KILLLEN8_DONE); len8logs/probe_base.raw and probe_W_len8.raw (both end LCAISALANE_DONE); LEN8_DETERMINATION.md; src/core/memory.c:839,:843-845; src/cpus/cpu_alpha_palcode.c:144</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcashiftub</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c: 0x800 &lt;&lt; dev with dev reaching 20 evaluates 2^31 in a signed 32-bit int -- undefined behaviour, in the loop the fork&#x27;s own comment treats as the safe path</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c: 0x800 &lt;&lt; dev with dev reaching 20 evaluates 2^31 in a signed 32-bit int -- undefined behaviour, in the loop the fork&#x27;s own comment treats as the safe path — commits: c7d7414 — witness: probe:regress/lca_confbus_probe.py against build-asan/gxemul -- UBSAN differential, HEAD 1 diagnostic -&gt; FIXED 0 (artifacts/lcashiftub/ubsan_HEAD_20260907.raw / ubsan_FIXED_20260907.raw) — note: FILED 2026-09-07, raised by the codex seat (regress/artifacts/lcabadval/codex_scoping_20260907.txt) and verified:
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:21598:repair 14 FULLY STAGED -- probe edits, contract, PRETABLE, check_pred.py, mutants_r14.py and a map-verified 15-leg driver, all ordered before any run. Three checkers green. NOTHING MEASURED; #530 table 7 still holds the machine, deliberately unraced. Next: fire table 12, then the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swaps Fable requires MEASURED, then the decline carriers</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 13a (the INTMASK and CONTROL-write label swaps the stop condition required MEASURED): CHECK13A_PASS -- base 204/204, M7_intmasklatch 201/204, M8_ctllatch 201/204, each exact against PRETABLE13a.out.  No INTMASK or CONTROL carrier owed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 14 (repair 15: the TIME and REV decline carriers, the entries 13-and-17 pair): CHECK14_PASS, 18 legs exact -- base 218/218 on probe f5e915f6; M3_timelatch and M5_revlatch 214/218 (were 204/204 escapes); M6/M7/M8 215/218; D_nodogclear 216/218.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 15a (pass 2&#x27;s finding): H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear 218/218, both escapes AS PREDICTED -- the HARD_RESET clear&#x27;s residue had no row; ENDIANESS disclosed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 16 (repair 16: the CONTROL arm&#x27;s residue-text count for each clear in both latch states): CHECK16_PASS, 25/25 legs exact on probe 5f770991 (226 rows) -- H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear now detected; W_istlb and W_imklb 226/226 as predicted (disclosed).  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — [EVIDENCE REPAIRED 2026-09-26 by #529: this entry cited `_scratchpad/fable_flagship_20260918.md (brief)`, a volatile brief, while the answer lived only in the transcript -- 87 claude-fable-5-1 turns, 0 refusals, a genuine seat answer.]  **RATIFY** the panel&#x27;s refutation of P2/P3 and the reshaped repair 14; **DISSENT on closure readiness -- two checkable defects sit in the working tree and ONE WOULD RED THE GATE TODAY.**  VERIFIED: `regress/gate_arm.sh`&#x27;s uncommitted hunk pins `crime_width rows run` at **188**, while every repair-14 leg since 09-17 08:34 reads **/204** -- a gate run on this tree reds three checks.  The pin must move to 204 in the same commit as the probe, AFTER the base leg (the `#462` rule).  VERIFIED: there is no `#529` commit at all, and `regress/crime_width_probe.py` is staged `A` but never committed; table 12 was aborted at leg 4 of 15 and re-fired, so the ruling&#x27;s own stop condition -- every enumerated mutant built and killed, the zero carried with its denominator -- is NOT met until that table completes. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/flagship_20260918/fable5_flagship_20260918_answer.txt (the answer, extracted from transcript agent-a2865c082138f4cf6; its brief beside it)</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-MEASURED-DESIGN-INVALID</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1-MEASURED-DESIGN-INVALID&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** VERDICT: DO NOT SHIP REPAIR 14 AS PROPOSED.  P2 IS FALSE AND P3 IS FALSE, AND IT MEASURED BOTH. SIX MUTANTS, TWO TABLES, PREDICTIONS MATCHED 6 OF 6. *** base 188/188 | PC_imk4r 187/188 reds `gate line&#x27; (POSITIVE CONTROL, reproducing close-8 exactly) | M1_gotolatch 178/188 KILLED on ten rows | **M2_ld278clr 188/188 ESCAPE** | M4_timeplain 184/188 (DISCRIMINATING CONTROL, exactly the four predicted rows) | **M3_timelatch 188/188 TOTAL ESCAPE**. **O1, THE FINDING OF THE ROUND: THE 56-CELL PRODUCT IS THE ACCEPT HALF OF A 112-CELL SPACE.**  It describes only accesses that are SERVICED.  The DECLINE arm -- the thing #529 ADDED -- has its own product {len 1,2} x {R,W} x {7 labels} x {latch}, and the enumeration contains NONE of it.  **Parts A and B are both accept-side, so NEITHER CAN REACH IT.**  This supersedes the deepseek-vs-codex disagreement entirely: they were arguing how to extend the accept-side product while the missing half was a different arm of the same `if&#x27;. **O2: P3 IS FALSE -- THE K-FORM IS LOUD, NOT SILENT.**  It falls into the decline arm, SETS the latch and PRINTS; it escapes because the announce is STOLEN (in `latch x5&#x27;&#x27;s prologue the count stays 1), not because it is absent.  The G-form is the silent one.  **My brief reasoned `it declines silently&#x27; and aimed the repair at value oracles -- reasoning from silence pointed the repair at the wrong channel.** **O3, the Q2 answer, MEASURED: a TWO-LINE edit scores 188/188** -- move `goto crime_declined&#x27; INSIDE the latch block and condition it on `relative_addr != CRIME_TIME&#x27;.  A narrow access at CRIME_TIME that is NOT its session&#x27;s first refusal falls into the switch and advances the guest clock, one of the four defects the fix&#x27;s own comment says the goto prevents.  The SAME edit without the latch conjunct (M4_timeplain) is killed 184/188 on exactly the four predicted rows -- ~2.2 million to one on the raw value -- and the liveness control reads `large&#x27; in BOTH runs, so the channel is live and the difference is the mutant.  **Part A cannot test this at all: a pre-latch session by construction contains no refusal before the cell under test.** **O4: the decline x latch-SET axis derived -- 7 cells, 2 OPEN (REV and TIME)**, on a discriminator that needs no run (does any session refuse at this label more than ONCE?).  *** AND THE PROBE ALREADY KNEW: crime_width_probe.py:1077-1079 states the asymmetry in as many words, derived for a DIFFERENT mutant, and nobody turned it around to ask what it implies for the goto. ***  Two rows in one diff close the axis. **O5: M2_ld278clr is a FIFTH escape and it CONFIRMS my buckets re-derivation independently** -- ACCEPTS entry 46 (ld +0x278) is one of the eight PRE-BLIND entries buckets8.py named, and the only one with neither an equivalence derivation nor a measurement.  The seat reached it by BUILDING A MUTANT; the deriver reached it by READING SESSIONS.  Two roads, same cell. **O6: Part A&#x27;s denominator is 8, not 23** (mirror14.py: N_ENTRIES_WITH_NO_PRELATCH_OBSERVER=8 of 46) -- matching BUCKETS8_rerun.out&#x27;s N_PRE_BLIND=8 exactly, from an independent tool. **O7: Q3 IS UNANSWERABLE AS POSED AND THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER SAYS SO** -- 2 of the 5 HOST-DIAGNOSTIC and 6 of the 10 EQUIVALENT cells have NO LISTED MEMBERS (crime_width_probe.py:242-257: `a bucket whose members cannot be listed cannot be audited&#x27;).  My brief promoted those counts to a SETTLED PREMISE while its own source flags them unlistable.  **8 of 46 cannot be checked by anyone**, so the nine-entry demand is a FLOOR rather than the answer. O8: four unnamed axes collapse with warrants (cpu-&gt;is_32bit is DEAD CODE on ip32 -- subtype 32 -&gt; R4400 -&gt; isa_level 3 -&gt; is_32bit == 0; ncpus; use_fb; physical_ram_in_mb).  **A DOMAIN DEPENDENCY NOBODY HAD STATED:** a real MIPS guest emits len in {1,2,4,8} exactly, but memory_rw.c:495-523 CLAMPS len at a device&#x27;s end and can emit 1..7 -- inert here ONLY because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8.  That makes codex&#x27;s reachability argument conditional on a constant rather than absolute.  Also: an accepted HARD_RESET write TERMINATES its session, so Part B costs one NEW SESSION per cell; and #529&#x27;s own diff created a stale citation -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:5574 cites dev_sgi_ip32.c:698, now :728. O9, ITS OWN ERRORS RECORDED BY THE SEAT RATHER THAN BY ME: a row-to-session off-by-one in its deriver (found pre-ship; buckets8.py unaffected), the backslash trap twice, and **a CRLF script that EXITED 0 HAVING BUILT AND RUN NOTHING** -- caught only because two seconds is impossible for two 17-minute probes.  No damage: the cd failed before the sentinel was dropped. FOOTPRINT CLEAN: no project tree written, all four fork copies still md5 8c1d1545..., clone sentinel cleared, source cmp-clean, binary -nt source, restored byte-identical to base. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/opus_pass1.md (30 KB) and opus_pass1_work/ -- PREDICT.md 23:58:36 and PREDICT2.md 00:04:17 against builds at 00:00:0x / 00:18:4x; six probe logs all ending CRIMEP_DONE; mirror14.py, mutants14.py, frozen drivers kill14.run-000006.sh / kill14b.run-001836.sh</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-REFIRE-ANSWERED</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1-REFIRE-ANSWERED&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — MANUAL — *** THE RE-FIRE WORKED: 353 KB streamed, ZERO content-filter flags, 7,826 b of verdict.  SAME SEAT, SAME QUESTIONS, SAME TREE -- only neutral vocabulary, reading scoped to src/ + regress/*.py, and the edit-construction question dropped.  The section-C5 remedy is validated a second time, on the seat it was minted from. ***  VERDICT: repair 14 needs a revised coverage model.  **ITS DEEPEST FINDING REFRAMES THE DOMAIN AND CUTS AGAINST THE OTHER SEATS&#x27; REMEDY**: adding lane and PROM-window state mechanically gives 224 nominal tuples, but that MISREPRESENTS REACHABILITY -- the MIPS producer checks natural alignment and the CRIME switch matches the EXACT offset, so every named label has the lane bit CLEAR and a 4-byte access to a register&#x27;s low lane reaches `default&#x27;.  The lane is NOT a free factor, so the corrected enumeration is REACHABILITY-CONSTRAINED rather than a cross-product -- meaning deepseek&#x27;s remedy (state the six-factor product) would have been wrong in the opposite direction.  Two seats pushed the enumeration opposite ways and the truth is neither.  **A RECORDS FINDING NO OTHER SEAT REACHED:** the shipped probe has NO direct value assertion for accepted CONTROL `lw +0x08&#x27; -- it runs through ACCEPTS where its destination is overwritten, `devsig hi&#x27; checks REV and `acc ctl ld&#x27; checks EIGHT-byte CONTROL -- so the equivalence derivation is sound but its claimed supporting row is missing.  That independently confirms the close-8 reading that table 11&#x27;s C_ctl4r leg was vacuous for want of an ORACLE rather than an ACCESS.  Also named four arms whose effects the common tail does NOT reproduce (DOG&#x27;s register effects, INTSTAT&#x27;s interrupt-LINE update, TIME&#x27;s update, REV&#x27;s PC effect), and independently enumerated the instrument at 51 sessions / 188 uniquely named rows -- a free cross-check on the denominator every score in this campaign is quoted against. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-16 — MANUAL — GO-WITH-CHANGES.  **FOUND F3, AND IT REFUTES A CLAIM OF MINE USING THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER.**  My brief said an early `return&#x27; in place of `goto crime_declined&#x27; would skip the interrupt recomputation and memory_writemax64, &#x27;a defect the shipped code does not have&#x27;.  crime_width_probe.py:269-272 says the opposite and gives the warrant: the two are EQUIVALENT on every channel because memory_rw pre-zeroes a device read buffer (#95) and nothing on a declined access writes HARDINT or SOFTINT, so the tail&#x27;s restore and recompute are identities -- measured 40/40 in kill table 1 and formally DISCLOSED.  UPHELD: the statements are mechanically skipped and the skipping is UNOBSERVABLE, so the consequence I attached is what is false.  I imported a correct general caution (the four-readers common-tail lesson) into the one site where it had been measured not to apply. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — MANUAL — NOT RATIFIED as written -- and the strongest answer of the panel.  It reached the 46-vs-56 finding INDEPENDENTLY and supplied the MECHANISM no other seat did: 23 is a count of ACCEPTS ENTRIES rowed post-latch by repair 13, not of product cells, and MANY ENTRIES MAP TO ONE CELL (the CONTROL writes 0x0201 / 0x0001 / 0 / 0x0200 / 0x0100 are five entries of ONE cell), which is why no re-count could ever reconcile 46 with 56.  **IT THEN DERIVED WHY INTSTAT 4R ESCAPES EVERYTHING**: using 23 as the class-closure denominator is how IST 4R falls through -- it is not in the 23 because the SET side is already pinned by `istat ctl&#x27;, and it is still open on CLEAR.  **THE MISSING FLOOR CELL, NAMED WITH ITS ORACLE REQUIREMENT: INTSTAT 4R, latch-CLEAR, with SOFTINT|HARDINT SEEDED NONZERO** -- sharper than my own criterion, which said `driven pre-refusal with an oracle&#x27; and did not say what the oracle must contain.  ADDS A DESIGN CONSTRAINT I had not stated: G_clr_imk4r 187/188 reddening `gate line&#x27; must STAY the positive control in the 188-row instrument, so the next closing pass keeps a CLEAR-half control that is not TIME -- repair 14 owes a check that it does not disturb it.  ALSO: P1 was NOT the full enclosing function; the omitted prelude at 229-235 (CONTROL = ENDIANESS 0x100 on every access) IS the warrant for the CONTROL-4R equivalence the packet asserted without it.  A section-D violation of mine. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **VERDICT: DO NOT RATIFY AS WRITTEN.**  *** AN UNREAD REVIEW ON AN IN-FLIGHT ROUND, RECORDED 2026-09-17 -- it answered on 2026-09-16 and had no cell until section G surfaced it. ***  Transport: `kimi-k3:cloud` SUBSTITUTE, so PACKET-FED; its claims are the packet&#x27;s, walked rather than re-derived from the tree. **IT WALKED THE ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN REASONING ABOUT IT, which is what the brief asked for and what makes its finding checkable:** `2x2x2x7 = 56` (seven case labels, six named plus `default`); `23 + 8 + 10 + 5 = 46`; *** therefore **56 - 46 = 10 CELLS APPEAR IN NO CATEGORY** ***.  It names the settling fact rather than guessing at the cause -- *the per-cell disposition table* -- and says plainly that the ACCEPTS-to-cell map is not settleable from the packet. **FINDING 1 -- THE PACKET CONTRADICTS ITSELF:** P4 claims *&quot;the latch-CLEAR state is driven by session 40 (`latch x5`) ALONE&quot;*, and P5&#x27;s own positive control disproves it -- `G_