d; NO row is owed.&quot;  X1 and X3 graded clause (e); its Q3 items 1-12 applied as r17, item 13&#x27;s records outside the probe landing with #529&#x27;s commit, r18 adding GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s r17 audit and the ACCEPTS-46 enumeration, r19 one docstring sentence from Astra&#x27;s second records audit (2026-09-28), and r20 the final ruling&#x27;s comment correction at ACCEPTS entry 21 plus the MEASURED/derived qualifier (2026-09-30), r21 the four text fixes of Astra&#x27;s confirmation of that ruling, and r22 one docstring qualifier the precommit hook&#x27;s score-claim check required (the committed text). — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/fable5_f2_adjudication.md — record: 2026-09-14 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 16:29:48Z (agent ae169fa9758283eaf) -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 2026-09-14T16:22:26Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8, keeping the seat&#x27;s identity line.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the file carries a dated provenance note since 2026-09-26; the first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  ADJUDICATION, LAST, on 8 of 9 mandated seats (agy not fired): REPAIR 11 -- ldP is a FLOOR breach (repair 10 crossed the window with 4R/4W/8W, so the fourth cell cannot be (e); six seats); A2 ENDIANESS is clause (e) (cleared, never branched) -- DISCLOSE, tuples licensed as (e) strengthening; A3/A5 DISCLOSE; A4/A6 killed.  Repair 11 owes a TARGETED table (the ~20 kills in rearm/latch x5) AND closing pass 6 (enumeration verification); the Opus aug run does not discharge it.  Overturned: 