e units: the FLOOR is the 23 open guest-visible cells (31 minus the 8 already pinned), NOT all 28 latch-SET mutants and NOT all 56 product cells** -- a mutant at an equivalent or pinned cell teaches nothing, a row at a cell no mutant reaches is unfalsifiable, so the floor is the INTERSECTION.  PRETABLE 11 carries the WHOLE product with per-cell disposition: 23 rowed, 8 already-pinned, 10 equivalent (no row), 5 host-diagnostic (clause-(e), disclosed with F1/F1b/F3&#x27;s measurements); 10+5+8+23 = 46.  Q3: table 11 AND closing pass 8, BOTH -- retyped rows are measured not assumed, and pass 8 VERIFIES the enumeration cell-by-cell and must close on a zero carried WITH its denominator.  D1&#x27;s grade was under-determined while D7 was punted and is now SECURED by it.  D3/D4 (the two disclosures I flagged) UPHELD, each verified against the seat&#x27;s measurements and each with an independent second reason.  L4 it names: its own RA3, and the header&#x27;s `46 kinds&#x27; vs `46 ENTRIES, not 46 kinds&#x27; inconsistency (grok&#x27;s nit, confirmed) -- both corrected in place. — record: 2026-09-17 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 06:25:19Z (agent a2bba4bc2896433b4) -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 2026-09-17T06:17:21Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8, keeping the seat&#x27;s identity line.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the file carries a dated provenance note since 2026-09-26; the first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  *** RULING: REPAIR 14 IS TWO EARNED CLASS-CLOSURES PLUS ONE FLOOR CELL -- NOT NINE CARRIERS AND NOT AN OPEN-ENDED HUNT.  SHIP IN ONE DIFF. *** **THE ONE SUBSTANTIVE OVERTURN NO SEAT REACHED, AND IT IS THE BEST THING IN THE ROUND: THE DECLINE FACE IS UNDER-MEASURED.**  `latch_label()&#x27; has run at exactly THREE of its five guest-observable labels -- INTSTAT (killed), TIME (escape), REV (escape) -- while **INTMASK and CONTROL-WRITE are DERIVED COVERED AND NEVER MEASURED**.  Fable&#x27;s own words: *building the two measured escapes and deriving the rest is the exact move (`derive instead of measure&#x27;) that M5_revlatch was built to punish.*  O4 DERIVED REV open and M5 MEASURED it open; deriving INTMASK/CONTROL-write COVERED is the same gamble in the other direction.  **Closure is not claimable until both swaps are built and scored by the M6 method.** Q1: adopts the Opus spine.  ACCEPT SIDE -- entry 21 in BOTH latch states, seeded above bit 31 (verified: +0x10 &amp; 4 == 0 takes the high lane at :294, so without the seed the row is `devsig hi&#x27; again, and POST is genuinely blind too since entry 21&#x27;s POST drivers [19, 26] are BOTH oracle-less); entries 32/33 via the clock-advance GAPPED channel; entry 46.  CUT AS EQUIVALENT with derivations into the contract: 1, 3 (REV is read nowhere -- Fable grepped: 5 hits, no consumer, prelude re-forces it), 4, 8 (4R high lane answers 0, and so does a decline).  Entry 40 -&gt; HOST-DIAGNOSTIC.  **It upholds that `nine&#x27; counted ENTRIES and spent them as ROWS.** **ENTRY 14 IS GRADED L2, NOT DEBT** -- `p acc ctl msg&#x27; counts the `sw&#x27; twin and not the `sd&#x27;: same address, same body-tested value, other width, no row.  *The #499 cell reproduced INSIDE the row that closed the #499 family.*  Entries 13/17 neither flat-included nor flat-filed: run the CHANNEL check, L2 if a body-tested-partition mutant escapes, clause (e) if the count cannot vary. A11 FOLDED INTO A12: the CONTROL 4R row is the ctl4r+ctl0c PAIR, never `lw +0x08&#x27; alone (vacuous, 0==0). Q2: ONE DIFF STANDS AND IT IS NOT #392.  The #392 test is *does each pass find a NEW class?* -- this chain does not: exactly TWO classes, each at TWO measured instances, both enumerations diff-closed.  STOP CONDITION in three parts: every enumerated mutant built and killed; the zero carried WITH ITS DENOMINATOR; the contract naming covered vs deliberately-not.  Terminates on the first clean sweep. Q3: THE NEW FLOOR CLAUSE IS **ADOPTED WITH THREE AMENDMENTS** -- (1) make it a THIRD DISJUNCT of the 2026-09-09 label clause rather than a standalone, because the carrier forbids two statements of one rule; (2) restrict to GUEST-OBSERVABLE SIDE EFFECT rather than `non-null body&#x27;, since the Opus wording would owe a row for default&#x27;s host-only debug(); (3) discharge is the label-swap mutant, folding the new axis into the existing measured-kill and CHANNEL machinery so nothing is new but the enumeration SOURCE.  Bounded to the labels of the ONE skipped dispatch in the enclosing function.  **And it carries its own expiry: minted from one device, so its first reuse elsewhere should CHECK the enumeration, not merely obey it** -- the freshly-minted-exemplar rule applied by the seat to its own ruling. Q4: upholds every reversal the panel forced (O1/112 withdrawn, O2&#x27;s redirect withdrawn, A11 vacuous, A13 self-applied to 1-of-2); keeps D1 OPEN as a CONDITION rather than a number; and **reverses NOTHING in the fix direction -- the goto de-fatalisation itself is unchallenged across two passes, and the entire dispute is detector coverage.** ORDER: (1) entry 14, sharpest and cheapest L2; (2) decline closure = TIME + REV carriers PLUS the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swap VERIFICATION; (3) accept closure = 21x2 seeded, 32/33, 46; (4) A11-&gt;A12 pair; (5) 13/17 after the CHANNEL check; (6) FILE A9&#x27;s kills, D1&#x27;s split-width routing, and the +2 translation. — record: 2026-09-17 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: this verification rested on the answer&#x27;s own `MODEL: claude-fable-5-1&#x27; line -- a SELF-REPORT, a check that cannot fail.  The subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py) shows the file was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 06:25:19Z (agent a2bba4bc2896433b4), after claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 2026-09-17T06:17:21Z.  The first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  *** SEAT VERIFIED AS FABLE, PER THE STANDING DIRECTIVE THAT A SUBAGENT CONFIRM FABLE USAGE RATHER THAN OPUS. ***  MODEL line reads `claude-fable-5-1&#x27; VERBATIM; liveness token present; VERDICT LINE FIRST; and the checker was asked explicitly whether the file is an ECHOED PROMPT rather than an answer -- it is not, it answers Q1-Q4 with reasoned dispositions.  That last check exists because this project once scored a 26,992-byte ECHOED BRIEF as the best answer in its panel. *** ONE MISMATCH, AND IT IS MINE, AND IT IS A GENUINE APPARATUS FINDING RATHER THAN A SEAT FAILURE. *** The ruling quotes CHECKPOINT.md&#x27;s first line as `2026-09-16 ~22:2x ...&#x27;; the file now reads `2026-09-17 ~01:2x ...&#x27;.  **I REFRESHED THE CHECKPOINT HEADER WHILE FABLE WAS STILL RUNNING**, so the quote is verbatim-correct for the file AS IT WAS WHEN THE SEAT READ IT, and I invalidated the seat&#x27;s own liveness proof underneath it.  Everything else in the line -- the HEAD stamp 9c91999 and the full trailing text -- matches exactly, which is what shows the seat really read the file. &gt; **THE RULE THIS BUYS: THE FILE-QUOTE LIVENESS CHECK REQUIRES THE QUOTED FILE TO BE STABLE FOR THE DURATION OF THE SEAT&#x27;S RUN.**  The echo test proves prompt delivery AND file access by asking for a verbatim quote -- and it silently stops proving the second half if the quoted file is edited mid-flight.  A mismatch then reads as a DEAD OR HALLUCINATING SEAT when the seat was neither.  Quote a file nothing in the round is going to touch, or freeze the quoted line for the run. *Caught only because the verifying subagent was told IN ADVANCE to distinguish a timestamp-only difference from a real failure -- had it not been, a correct Fable ruling would have been recorded as failing its own liveness check.* — record: 2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] The re-ruling&#x27;s first firing was written by claude-opus-4-8 after a refusal by claude-fable-5-1 (agent_models.py); kept as evidence, relabelled, never counted as the seat. — record: 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] The flagship&#x27;s first answer on repair 15&#x27;s pass 2 was written by claude-opus-4-8 after two refusals by claude-fable-5-1 (agent_models.py); relabelled, never counted as the seat.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — repair 13&#x27;s 23 / 8 / 10 / 5 is reproduced exactly, and every member now has a name. The two unnamed HOST-DIAGNOSTIC members are entries 11 and 15 (CONTROL 0x0001, 4W and 8W). The six unnamed EQUIVALENT members are 12, 13, 16, 17, 43 and 44 (CONTROL writes of 0, 0x0200 and 0x0100). The counts no longer describe r17, though. Now: 31 GUEST-VISIBLE (30 rowed in both latch states; entry 34, `sd +0x40`, rowed only with the latch SET); 4 ROWED on the CONTROL-text count in both states (10, 11, 14, 15); 1 HOST-DIAGNOSTIC ONLY (40); 10 EQUIVALENT. All 92 entry x latch cells were MEASURED, and 92 of 92 matched predictions written before any run. — #529 the Opus 5 MEASURING seat on the contract&#x27;s ACCEPTS-46 buckets (GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation of the 09-25 re-ruling asked for an L4 enumeration with justified dispositions).  Verbatim verdict: repair 13&#x27;s 23 / 8 / 10 / 5 is reproduced exactly, and every member now has a name. The two unnamed HOST-DIAGNOSTIC members are entries 11 and 15 (CONTROL 0x0001, 4W and 8W). The six unnamed EQUIVALENT members are 12, 13, 1