his row as discharged): NOT FIRED -- the kimi seat sat outside the owner&#x27;s 2026-10-17 roster; nothing was sent.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-18 — #527 CLOSURE check: DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED -- a records question that needs the rows&#x27; files opened, and GLM is packet-fed.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-18 — #527 CLOSURE check (which closed this row as discharged): NOT FIRED -- GLM 5.3 is the roster&#x27;s one packet-fed seat, and even it was not fired here -- a records question needs the files.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-18 — #527 CLOSURE check (which closed this row as discharged): NOT FIRED -- minimax-m3 was given no packet; the owner&#x27;s 2026-10-17 roster, not a wall.</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-10-18 — awaiting fable5 — ppcgateimageskip [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5] closed as discharged in #527&#x27;s closure-records commit and owes the REGRESS review, a distinct phase under the regress-is-fable-only directive, batched to the flagship sign-off.  The question is in the row&#x27;s hold_question.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armmsrmodekill</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm.c: ONE privileged guest MSR (MSR CPSR_c,#0x14 = 0xE321F014) ends the emulator PROCESS at arm_load_register_bank()&#x27;s default: -- a reserved M[4:0] is UNPREDICTABLE, not fatal</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">cpu_arm.c: ONE privileged guest MSR (MSR CPSR_c,#0x14 = 0xE321F014) ends the emulator PROCESS at arm_load_register_bank()&#x27;s default: -- a reserved M[4:0] is UNPREDICTABLE, not fatal — commits: 4f908ad5 — #562 CLOSES.  msr_imm, arm_pop&#x27;s ^ restore and the DPI S-to-PC restore decline the MODE FIELD of a value naming a mode this model does not bank (the rest applies), announced once per site per CPU; Save/Load&#x27;s default: arms are latched backstops (no exit(1)).  An emulator POLICY for UNPREDICTABLE (DDI 0100I A2.5.7), not architecture; codex&#x27;s whole-operation dissent recorded.  The detector (arm_msrmode_probe.py, 47 rows, 43 sessions, a generated grid) took five repairs; repair 5&#x27;s tables: 110 runs, 104 distinct mutants, 103 red, M_msr_argmask disclosed.  The final pass&#x27;s latch-clear residue and two measured closures are filed (armmsrmodedebt) by owner ruling 2026-10-09.  Gate 14: run 1 caught a STALE dev_i80321.o (#562 grew struct arm_cpu; the build tracks no header dependencies) -- every build tree rebuilt clean, run 2 PASS, 1110 of 1110.  Filed: armusrstop, armspsrthumb, armmmuvehicle, armmsrmodedebt, headerstaleobj.  GPT-6 Astra (ultra) confirmed with changes (13), all records corrections, all applied.  Fable 5.1 was deliberately not fired on any pass (owner, 2026-10-07); badge A: the main loop (Opus 5.5) adjudicated each pass.  After the owner lifted the hold, Fable 5.1 adjudicated the main loop&#x27;s nine rulings before the commit, 2026-10-09 (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/fable_adjudication_20261009/fable5_adjudication562.md): RATIFY WITH CHANGES (3), all nine upheld, the three records corrections applied. — witness: probe:regress/arm_msrmode_probe.py -- rung 3 on HEAD ef577140&#x27;s unmodified -E testarm: the 17-row witness 14/17 (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/witness_20261007/run_head.out: kill 14, kill 15, save 2s dead, every control green); the shipped 47-row detector 18/47 on HEAD with 29 named reds, and 47/47 on the fix (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/killtable5_20261008/run_head.out, run_fixed.out) — note: [2026-10-09] #562 SHIPPED -- the commits field is owed to the next commit, with the pass-2 receipt.  CORRECTION (GPT-6 Astra item 4, Fable 5.1 R9): the IN WORK note below calls M_msr_argmask &#x27;the cached-translation write, which NO stepping row can see&#x27; -- FALSE: none of the SHIPPED 47 rows sees it, but the filed loop prototype does (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/probe48.py, KTR5_LANE5.out 47/48); the old text is kept below.  || #562 IN WORK 2026-10-07: rung-3 witness regress/arm_msrmode_probe.py HEAD 16/26 -&gt; fixed 26/26; 20-mutant table 0 escapes (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/killtable_20261007/).  Pass 2 found two floor families (latch never revisited; SPSR source labels SVC-only) -&gt; repair + 36-mutant table running; the repair owes its own pass 2.  Fable 5.1 deliberately not fired (owner, 2026-10-07).  Opus 5.5 pass 2 (artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2_20261007/, measured): SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, 3 floor breaches -- F1 latch-line deletions 26/26 at MSR/POP/DPI/LOAD; F2 NEW `mask &amp;= ~0x0f` 26/26 (all driven MSR values have bit 4 set; `kill 03` row owed); F3 restore-mode axis SVC-only.  All three sent to the repair.  REPAIR (fix2, probe 26-&gt;38 rows) applied 2026-10-07 ~23:00: tables 2+3 all 36+6 new mutants red, 0 escapes.  Repair&#x27;s own pass 2 (panel_20261007_230103, copied to artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_pass2r_20261007): codex DO-NOT-SHIP (5 static breaches: return_flag / DPI PC-dest / DPI S enclosing predicates; label x latch at both restores), grok DO-NOT-SHIP (restore mode-keep mask bits 0/1/3 unpinned -- same CLASS as Opus F2; pop x zero-SPSR; Load backstop comment still false; I/F contract overclaim), deepseek DO-NOT-SHIP (spsr_copied gate), glm + kimi-k3:cloud SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, agy + minimax SHIP; kimi CLI 403 (subscription) -&gt; covered by kimi-k3:cloud.  All predictions sent to the Opus 5.5 seat to MEASURE.  Same class twice (mask width; latch x label) -&gt; next repair owes CLASS CLOSURE.  Opus 5.5 MEASURED the repair (artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r_20261007/): 21 of 23 mutants 38/38 -- helper ARM_FLAG_MODE-&gt;0xff (one token; declines msr cpsr_c,#0xd2), restore mask width x7, label x latch x outcome x6, I forced on decline x2, enclosing predicates x3 (return_flag, DPI rd==PC, non-S restore); killed: msr_imm ~0x1e (34/38), spsr_copied deleted (37/38).  Panel predictions CONFIRMED (grok, codex); agy + minimax SHIP votes refuted by measurement.  #499 pattern -&gt; REPAIR 3 = CLASS CLOSURE (A values/bits with I/F set, SPSR 0xcf/0xdf; B 40-cell label x latch x outcome; C enclosing-predicate session; D records) dispatched 2026-10-08.  REPAIR 3 (class closure) APPLIED 2026-10-08 ~06:3x: probe 40 rows; fixed 40/40, HEAD 17/40; 65 mutants (Opus&#x27;s 23 + earlier 42) ALL red (artifacts killtable3_20261008/); product code = comments only vs repair 2; build trees 24/24 two-part clear.  Its pass 2 FIRED (brief PASS2R3_brief_20261008.md, shared findings + 9 dispositions) + Opus seat measuring.  Repair-3 pass 2 (artifacts panel_pass2r3_20261008): codex DO-NOT-SHIP 2 + grok DO-NOT-SHIP 1 (static) -- helper projection widened to undriven bits (0x3f, |C; driven upper union 0xc00000c0) and decline flag provenance (old CPSR N/Z already equals SPSR N/Z at every decline); glm/deepseek/kimi-k3 SHIP-WITH-CHANGES; agy/minimax SHIP; kimi CLI 403.  Backstop comments now ratified by codex + grok.  Sent to the Opus seat to MEASURE.  Opus 5.5 MEASURED repair 3 (artifacts opus_pass2r3_20261008/): 14/20 fix-side mutants 40/40 -- helper projection width (0x3f, |C), decline flag provenance x7, S-instance enclosing cells (DPI rd==PC under S; pop return_flag||s_bit); its 42-row closure probe kills all 14.  Owner ruling 2026-10-08: close, one more review pass, commit.  REPAIR 4 dispatched (adopt Opus probe, closure rule: every operand bit set in an accept per path; every restored bit differs between sources at each decline; full 85-mutant re-table).  REPAIR 4 DONE 2026-10-08 ~15:4x (artifacts killtable4_20261008/): product code unchanged (fix4 == fix3); probe 43 rows (Opus closure probe + `msr wide`); fixed 43/43, HEAD 17/43; 91 mutants ALL red, none equivalent; closure rule checked per path.  FINAL pass 2 FIRED (PASS2R4_brief_20261008.md) + Opus measuring.  FINAL pass on repair 4 (artifacts panel_pass2r4_20261008): codex DO-NOT-SHIP 3 + grok DO-NOT-SHIP 1 (static) -- helper NARROWED by bit 3 (`&amp; 0x17` admits 0x18-0x1a; no driven value crosses that boundary), decline FORCING a constant (e.g. `| ARM_FLAG_N`; the old/new-differ rule does not catch forcing the expected polarity), msr decline bit narrowed at one label (20/30 label x bit cells), pop enclosing cell non-S/no-PC; records: &#x27;at EVERY decline&#x27; false for T, 0xffffffd1 bits 3:1 clear, inline c00000df comments stale.  glm/deepseek/minimax/kimi-k3 SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, agy SHIP, kimi CLI 403.  Opus measuring the same candidates.  Opus MEASURED on repair 4 (partial, 16:14): 4/4 escape 43/43 -- H_narrow_17, M_msr_clr0f_iaus, N_pop_Tlatch, N_dpi_forceN.  Owner ruling 2026-10-08: REPAIR 5 = GENERATED full grid (bit x polarity x path x outcome; msr label x bit; helper boundary values; pop 4 enclosing cells), one review pass, commit.  Dispatched.  Opus final measurement on repair 4 (artifacts opus_pass2r4_20261008/): 18 mutants, 15 escape 43/43 in 4 classes (A helper narrowing H_narrow_17 + H_case_18; B msr decline width per label x4; C restore forced/OR-ed bits x4; D T while latched x4) + M_msr_argmask; 3 controls killed.  All fed to repair 5&#x27;s second table.  REPAIR 5 (generated grid) MEASURED 2026-10-09 (artifacts killtable5_20261008/): 47 rows, 43 sessions; fixed 47/47, HEAD 18/47 (29 reds); 110 runs / 104 distinct mutants (the earlier set + Opus&#x27;s 18), 103 red, ONE escape: M_msr_argmask 47/47 -- the cached-translation write, which NO stepping row can see: debugger() clears every dyntrans translation when it interacts, so each re-execution is re-translated.  Repair 5&#x27;s NOT CLAIMED said the grid pinned the register form -- FALSE; corrected comment-only (AST-identical to the measured probe) and installed.  The helper agent hit the Opus weekly limit after the tables finished; results collected from its clone.  Final pass next.  FINAL pass on repair 5 (artifacts panel_pass2r5_20261009): grok SHIP-WITH-CHANGES 0 floor breaches (records: G1&#x27;s lead sentence false; PRETABLE5 sec.2 superseded; gate MEASURED placeholder); codex DO-NOT-SHIP 1 class, STATIC: a latch-CLEAR decline forcing a bit 31:8 at DPI/pop unobserved (48 of 72 cells), against the contract&#x27;s &#x27;forcing ... with the latch clear or set&#x27;; deepseek DO-NOT-SHIP (M_msr_argmask loop row owed); glm/agy/kimi-k3 SHIP-WITH-CHANGES; minimax SHIP; kimi CLI 403.  M_msr_argmask: grok + codex grade DISCLOSURE under the bounded DEPENDS-ON rule, deepseek owed.  Codex&#x27;s prediction sent to the Opus seat to MEASURE; owner to be asked before any repair 6.  || filed 2026-09-17 from a VOLUNTEERED grok side-finding (raised under the standing license while it was refuting a different brief), then CONFIRMED on a second firing by a full instruction-to-switch trace.  ONE ROUND, MEMBER 3 at BOTH default: arms.  *** SAVE (:559) IS NOT FIRST-HIT -- it runs on the OLD mode (SVC32, modelled) and returns; the process dies in LOAD (:606).  A LOAD-ONLY fix CREATES the Save kill, which is sibling parity and not a second row. ***  Member 1 DELETE is WRONG (leaves cpsr reserved and r[] on the previous bank -&gt; silent wrong-bank execution, then a second kill).  Member 5 FAULT is AVAILABLE on ARM but wrong: MSR is &#x27;Exceptions: None&#x27;.  THE DECLINE MUST SIT BEFORE SAVE, or roll cpsr back in Load -- callers write cpsr BETWEEN save and load.  RANKED ABOVE armthumbabortkill: process death vs running=0, cheaper witness, no fake-green hazard.  GATE 14&#x27;s 358 checks never feed the encoding.  *** REWRITE, NOT PATCH.  THE 16-ROW SPEC PLUS EIGHT AMENDMENTS DOES NOT CLOSE, AND THE SEAT THAT WROTE THE ORIGINAL SPEC RULED AGAINST ITS OWN WORK WHEN ASKED TO BE HARDER ON IT. ***  I asked plainly whether eight amendments on a 16-row spec meant the spec should be rewritten rather than patched, and named the `#392` shape as the thing I feared.  Answer: yes.  &#x27;A builder applying them in order will get 1+6 wrong and will either treat `save 2s` as a duplicate of `kill 15` or REPLACE `kill 15` with it, losing the `== 0x14` pin.&#x27;  *** AND THE TALLY ITSELF WAS A FROZEN NUMBER: it is 14/17 -&gt; 17/17 over THIRTEEN sessions, not 14/16 -&gt; 16/16 over twelve.  The original 12 was already false -- 16 scored minus `enc ok` minus the identity row minus one for live/pc/armed sharing S1 is 13, and the spec wrote 12. ***  THE VEHICLE STANDS and is unchanged: `-V -A -E testarm -M 64`, `0xE321F014`, member 3 at BOTH `default:` arms, one fresh process per scored row that executes a guest instruction, mid-stream dump.  The ROW LIST, the ORACLES and the SESSION ARITHMETIC are replaced. **ANSWER TO MY INTERACTION QUESTION 1+6, AND IT REFUTES MY FRAMING.**  I asked whether, once amendment 1 makes EOF-alone the kill trigger, the `enc ok` / `no cbit` / dump-before-MSR machinery becomes THE ONLY THING between the witness and a false green.  The answer is that those three are **NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT** -- each has a smallest defeat: dump-DEST proves MRS ran, not that the MSR word was planted or stepped; `no cbit` is greened by a decoder that never writes the mode field AT ALL, which greens every kill row too; and `enc ok` walking a constructor instead of the planted literal is the BFX incident repeating.  What actually closes false-green, all four required: (1) **POST want is `m=13 sp once`, not `m=13`** -- member 3 prints `(once)`, and encoding-nop, skipped-step and a silent member-2 all print nothing, so the latch must be IN the got string or its absence is a comment rather than a FAIL; (2) **poison `DEST+4` with 0xdeadbeef** and dump DEST+4, never DEST+0, so a never-fired post-MSR store reds; (3) **one `WORDS` dict**, with every `put w` drawn from it and a per-session plant-dump of the MSR slot -- this is the load-bearing anti-false-green that amendment 6 hoped `enc ok` was; (4) **named-red tally** -- HEAD must be EXACTLY the three named reds, because 17/17 on HEAD is not success. **ANSWER TO INTERACTION 3+5, AND AMENDMENT 3 IS HALF-RIGHT AND MISREADS ITS OWN CASE.**  The original two reds were `kill 14` and `kill 15` -- TWO LOAD HOLES catching the `== 0x14` special case -- **not** Load vs Save, which is what amendment 3 assumed.  So: SCORE `save 2s`, KEEP `kill 15`, do NOT replace one with the other.  The underlying worry stands: without a scored two-write row a Load-only skip-memcpy POSTs clean and still dies on the write OUT of reserved mode (16/17, `save 2s` red on the second MSR -- that is the point of the row). **AMENDMENT 5 IS TRUE OF THE ENCODING AND INERT FOR THIS PROBE, VERIFIED LOCALLY BY ME AND NOT TAKEN FROM THE SEAT:** `#0x14` does clear I and F, and testarm does hang cons/ether/rtc off `irqc` -- but ARM IRQ dispatch sits inside `if (!single_step) {` at `cpu_dyntrans.c:206` with the ARM arm at `:208-209`, and `-V` sets single_step; **`fiq_asserted` has ZERO occurrences across all of `src/`** and `ARM_FLAG_F` zero in `cpu_dyntrans.c`, so there is no ARM FIQ dispatch to enable; and debugger interaction `timer_stop()`s so `step N` runs no host-timer callback.  **The pin is STAY ON `step`, NEVER `continue`** -- a `continue` after a LANDED `#0x14` can take `arm_exception` and run Save on the reserved current mode, which is a free-run hazard and not a step hazard.  DO NOT change the filed stimulus to `#0xD4`. **BOTH KILL ARMS CONFIRMED AT HEAD BY READING:** `cpu_arm.c:559-561` `arm_save_register_bank: unimplemented mode %i` + `exit(1)`, and `:606-608` the same for `arm_load_register_bank`.  Two arms, two kills -- which is exactly why member 3 is owed at both and why `save 2s` is independent rather than a duplicate. **DROPPED FROM THE ORIGINAL SPEC:** EOF-AND-text as the kill trigger; the 12 sessions; &#x27;two reds because two default: arms&#x27;; POST `0xd3` on `kill 14` (member 3 refuses the MODE FIELD, so I|F stay clear at `0x13` -- record I|F, do not want them); already-USR32 as the fake-green mechanism; copy-flags-`session()`; copy-flags-`printed()` (arm_flags_probe.py has none).  Amendment 8 belongs on the ALPHA spec, not this one. **CLAUSE (e), DISCLOSED NOT ROWED:** register-form MSR (`X(msr)` copies rm into arg[0] and calls msr_imm); the 26-bit holes; the other 32-bit holes 0x16/18/19/1a/1c/1d/1e (`kill 14` + `kill 15` catch a ONE-VALUE special case, not a two-value one); SPSR-then-`MOVS pc`; free-run IRQ after a landed reserved write, pinned by stay-on-step. **BUILD FROM THE ARTIFACT, NOT FROM THIS NOTE** -- the complete 17-row table, the 13-session schedule, the CONTROL=DEAD set, the plant layouts and the tally live verbatim at `regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/WITNESSSPEC_REWRITE_grok_20260917.txt`.  Transcribing a row table into a ledger note is the frozen-number class waiting to happen. **ONE BUILD REQUIREMENT I FOUND MYSELF AND THE SPEC DOES NOT STATE:** the launch line uses `regress/arm_bfx_stub.bin`, which is on the NEVER-STAGE list and is UNTRACKED.  That is safe, and the reason matters -- **all 11 top-level committed probes referencing such a stub CREATE IT IF ABSENT** (e.g. `alpha_harness_probe.py:169-173`).  `arm_msrmode_probe.py` MUST carry the same self-create block, or it will be the one committed probe that cannot run on a fresh clone.  *** THE PROBE WAS ATTACKED BEFORE IT WAS EVER RUN, AND IT HAD THREE INDEPENDENT DEFECTS. Verdict: &#x27;It runs.  It does not score.&#x27; ***  (1) **LINE LABELS ARE 16-BYTE ALIGNED** -- `debugger_cmds.c:709` is `addr = addr_start &amp; ~0xf`, so `dump 0x9004` labels the line `0x00009000` AND BLANK-PADS the leading word groups, shifting every group index.  (2) **THE DUMP RENDERS LITTLE-ENDIAN BYTES, NOT A WORD** -- 0x2a prints as `2a000000`.  (3) **`save 2s` READ A SLOT NOTHING WROTE**: its plant put SP at DEST+16 via `str_sp_10` while `classify()` read DEST+8, so ` sp` could NEVER appear and **the row was ALWAYS RED, pre-fix and post-fix alike** -- not a witness of Save at all. *** THE REMEDIES FOR (1) AND (2) ALREADY EXISTED IN THIS TREE AND I DID NOT USE THEM: `arm_bdt_probe.py:123-149` records the alignment measurement from 2026-09-11 in a seven-line comment, and `arm_flags_probe.py:191-193` carries `sw()` for the byte order. Knowledge present, unconsulted at the moment of use -- the carrier&#x27;s own recurring finding.  The repair COPIES both rather than inventing. *** **AND THE FAILURE MODE WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN A FALSE GREEN, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING.**  `live` wants 0x2a and would have got 0x2a000000; `armed` would have given `?/?`.  Both sit in the CONTROL=DEAD set, so the probe would have printed `ARMMSRMODE_CONTROL=DEAD`, `RESULT=0/0` and &#x27;SETUP FAILED -- NOT no defect&#x27;.  **The vehicle-kill design worked exactly as intended: it would have REFUSED TO SCORE rather than lying.**  That is the difference between a wasted run and a wrong record, and it is why the CONTROL=DEAD set is not decoration. *A self-check while repairing it showed why `arm_flags_probe.py` warns as it does: `deadbeef` read RAW yields 0xdeadbeef, so the POISON comparison would have MATCHED under the broken parser while every real value was wrong -- the sentinel&#x27;s own byte pattern hiding the defect.* **ONE CORRECTION RUNNING THE OTHER WAY, against the SPEC rather than the probe:** `print pc` wanting CODE+8 after `step 2` is RIGHT; the spec table&#x27;s CODE+4 is the wrong half, and a builder must not &#x27;fix&#x27; the probe down to it.  REPAIRED, AST clean, zero raw `dump` commands left.  **STILL NOT RUN** -- the adjudicated ship order puts the commit first, then this.  *** THE RANKING IS SETTLED BY READING WITH A DENOMINATOR: `ip30abortkill` FIRST. ***  And the distinction that settles it is worth more than the verdict: **the gap on ip30 is &#x27;we do not run that OS here&#x27;; the gap on armmsr is &#x27;that OS would not do this.&#x27;  Only the second kind of gap demotes a defect.**  A process death on the documented interrupt path of the guest the machine exists to run outranks a process death that requires the guest to program a reserved mode. **Q1 -- CAN A REAL ARM GUEST REACH `armmsrmodekill`?  NO.**  `arm_save_register_bank` / `arm_load_register_bank` switch on `cpsr &amp; 0x1f`: **7 arms handled, 25 of 32 unhandled.**  Handled: USR32 0x10, FIQ32 0x11, IRQ32 0x12, SVC32 0x13, ABT32 0x17, UND32 0x1b, SYS32 0x1f. The unhandled 25 break down as: **26-bit modes 0x00-0x03** (`cpu_arm.h` names them and `grep -c &#x27;case ARM_MODE_USR26&#x27;` across src/ is ZERO; CATS/testarm/barearm are SA-110/SA1110 and the in-tree NetBSD `armreg.h` does not even define 26-bit modes); **0x04-0x0F unused**; **0x14/0x15/0x18/0x19/0x1c/0x1d/0x1e reserved** -- DDI 0100I A2.5.7 says *&#x27;If any other value is programmed into the mode bits M[4:0], the result is UNPREDICTABLE&#x27;*, and there are NO MSR exceptions; **0x16 Monitor** (TrustZone, not on any in-tree CPU); **0x1a Hyp** (ARMv7-A virt, likewise). A real kernel writes the named constants plus I/F -- `msr cpsr_c, #PSR_SVC32_MODE|I32_bit|F32_bit` (0xD3), IRQ 0x12, USR on process start, SYS for some copy paths -- and locore is `bic r0,r0,#0x1f ; orr r0,r0,#&lt;legal&gt; ; msr cpsr_c,r0`.  **Userspace cannot do it at all**: `X(msr_imm)` strips the c-byte in USR32 (`mask &amp;= 0xff000000`). **Q2 -- THE SECOND PATH, which I had not considered and which is the one that could have been worse:** `MSR SPSR` is UNVALIDATED, and `MOVS PC, LR` / `LDM {..,pc}^` copies SPSR into CPSR **with no mode check**, after which Load dies identically.  But a correct kernel&#x27;s SPSR is either the CPSR saved at exception entry (a legal mode) or a sigreturn frame, and Linux&#x27;s `valid_user_regs` rejects anything whose MODE_MASK is not USR/USR26 and forces USR32.  **So the path exists and no correct kernel drives it.** **CONSEQUENCE FOR `armmsrmodekill`:** it stays a real process death and a real fix -- a hostile or buggy guest reaches it, and 25 of 32 encodings are unhandled -- but its SEVERITY is now measured rather than assumed, and it does NOT outrank ip30.  **`highrankunmeasured` is answered on the armmsr side by READING; the ip30 side stands as measured (gate_asan_sweep runs ip30 green, so the aborts are on no in-tree path).**</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** THE RANKING IS SETTLED BY READING WITH A DENOMINATOR: `ip30abortkill` FIRST. ***  And the distinction that settles it is worth more than the verdict: **the gap on ip30 is &#x27;we do not run that OS here&#x27;; the gap on armmsr is &#x27;that OS would not do this.&#x27;  Only the second kind of gap demotes a defect.**  A process death on the documented interrupt path of the guest the machine exists to run outranks a process death that requires the guest to program a reserved mode. **Q1 -- CAN A REAL ARM GUEST REACH `armmsrmodekill`?  NO.**  `arm_save_register_bank` / `arm_load_register_bank` switch on `cpsr &amp; 0x1f`: **7 arms handled, 25 of 32 unhandled.**  Handled: USR32 0x10, FIQ32 0x11, IRQ32 0x12, SVC32 0x13, ABT32 0x17, UND32 0x1b, SYS32 0x1f. The unhandled 25 break down as: **26-bit modes 0x00-0x03** (`cpu_arm.h` names them and `grep -c &#x27;case ARM_MODE_USR26&#x27;` across src/ is ZERO; CATS/testarm/barearm are SA-110/SA1110 and the in-tree NetBSD `armreg.h` does not even define 26-bit modes); **0x04-0x0F unused**; **0x14/0x15/0x18/0x19/0x1c/0x1d/0x1e reserved** -- DDI 0100I A2.5.7 says *&#x27;If any other value is programmed into the mode bits M[4:0], the result is UNPREDICTABLE&#x27;*, and there are NO MSR exceptions; **0x16 Monitor** (TrustZone, not on any in-tree CPU); **0x1a Hyp** (ARMv7-A virt, likewise). A real kernel writes the named constants plus I/F -- `msr cpsr_c, #PSR_SVC32_MODE|I32_bit|F32_bit` (0xD3), IRQ 0x12, USR on process start, SYS for some copy paths -- and locore is `bic r0,r0,#0x1f ; orr r0,r0,#&lt;legal&gt; ; msr cpsr_c,r0`.  **Userspace cannot do it at all**: `X(msr_imm)` strips the c-byte in USR32 (`mask &amp;= 0xff000000`). **Q2 -- THE SECOND PATH, which I had not considered and which is the one that could have been worse:** `MSR SPSR` is UNVALIDATED, and `MOVS PC, LR` / `LDM {..,pc}^` copies SPSR into CPSR **with no mode check**, after which Load dies identically.  But a correct kernel&#x27;s SPSR is either the CPSR saved at exception entry (a legal mode) or a sigreturn frame, and Linux&#x27;s `valid_user_regs` rejects anything whose MODE_MASK is not USR/USR26 and forces USR32.  **So the path exists and no correct kernel drives it.** **CONSEQUENCE FOR `armmsrmodekill`:** it stays a real process death and a real fix -- a hostile or buggy guest reaches it, and 25 of 32 encodings are unhandled -- but its SEVERITY is now measured rather than assumed, and it does NOT outrank ip30.  **`highrankunmeasured` is answered on the armmsr side by READING; the ip30 side stands as measured (gate_asan_sweep runs ip30 green, so the aborts are on no in-tree path).** — evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/REACH_grok_20260917.txt; src/cpus/cpu_arm.c:559,606; cpu_arm.h mode names</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — CONFIRMED — VERDICT: RATIFY WITH CHANGES (3).  All nine main-loop rulings UPHELD on the rules as written and the evidence re-checked: R1 member 3 at the complete set of guest CPSR.M writers (CPS decodes only as NOPs); R2 the backstops are reachable only after a debugger cpsr= plant; R3 the decline edits the local mask, never ic-&gt;arg[]; R4 no early return, new_cpsr used for the bank switch; R5 the probe AST-identical to all frozen copies (its own hash), 110 runs / 104 distinct / 103 red re-counted; R6 none of the final pass&#x27;s eight escapes is a FLOOR cell -- the five restore escapes act on bits 31:8 (single-operand marginals), the label x latch x bit residue is a disclosable two-axis joint, the two msr cells are label-conditioned where the switch lives in callees, M_msr_argmask adds a side effect and weakens no dominating predicate; the only breach was of the CONTRACT (clause e), repaired comment-only as (e) permits; R7 the stale dev_i80321.o scope; R8 the filed rows; R9 Astra&#x27;s corrections.  THREE CHANGES, applied before the commit: (1) Astra item 4 survived in the staged state_note -- corrected by the closing prefix; (2) the round&#x27;s records said Fable was not fired -- a sentence added to the CHANGELOG block, the commit message and the closure note; (3) PRETABLE5.out&#x27;s first-line mtime claim is void since its 08:13 append -- a dated clause in its CORRECTIONS.  Also taken: kimi-k3&#x27;s &#x27;new default: behaviour&#x27; ELSE checked FALSE (a CHANGELOG clause); gate_arm.sh&#x27;s `rows failed` grep is green only because note[:64] cuts the kill 14 note before &#x27; FAIL &#x27; (a latent FALSE RED, the safe direction) -&gt; armmsrmodedebt.  Noted for floodclass, not owed here: unlatched guest-drivable fatal()s in bdt_load (&#x27;s-bit: in usermode?&#x27;) and arm_exception (&#x27;Exception caused no mode change?&#x27;), and the latent ARM_EXCEPTION_TO_MODE[5] = 0. — evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/fable_adjudication_20261009/fable5_adjudication562.md; regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/fable_adjudication_20261009/FABLE_adjudication_brief_20261009.md — record: 2026-09-18 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  No panel was ever convened on this row.  The four recorded entries (deepseek, glm, grok, minimax) cite NO panel dir: they are remarks those seats volunteered about `armmsrmodekill` while answering some other round&#x27;s brief, recorded 2026-09-18 by the unread-seat sweep so the findings are not lost.  Recording them is what took this stage from ABSENT to 4/9 and reddened both stage gates -- the gate fired because the RECORD improved, not because a panel ran short.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — #562 the final pass (repair 5), the Opus 5.5 measuring seat (Agent tool; claude-opus-5-5 by agent_models.py): VERDICT: SHIP-WITH-CHANGES | 1 floor breach.  The breach is clause (e), the contract.  Product code is unchanged and still correct.  Codex&#x27;s prediction is CONFIRMED by measurement: a decline that forces N on the FIRST (latch-CLEAR) DPI or pop restore scores 47/47.  Two more edits do the same: OR-ing  Recorded seat by seat on 2026-10-09: the answer was read and adjudicated during the round (#562&#x27;s CHANGELOG block, the final pass (repair 5)) but had not been entered in the ledger. — evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/opus_pass2r5.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — #562 the final pass (repair 5) -- this seat&#x27;s answer, verbatim excerpt: &quot;- Insert the section **before `gate_end`**. That function returns a status; appending checks afterward can overwrite the failure status and print the verdict prematurely.&quot;.  Recorded seat by seat on 2026-10-09: read and adjudicated during the round (#562&#x27;s CHANGELOG block, the final pass (repair 5)), not entered in the ledger until now. — evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_pass2r5_20261009/codex.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — #562 the final pass (repair 5) -- this seat&#x27;s answer, verbatim excerpt: &quot;VERDICT: SHIP-WITH-CHANGES | 0 floor breaches&quot;.  Recorded seat by seat on 2026-10-09: read and adjudicated during the round (#562&#x27;s CHANGELOG block, the final pass (repair 5)), not entered in the ledger until now. — evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_pass2r5_20261009/agy.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — #562 the final pass (repair 5) -- this seat&#x27;s answer, verbatim excerpt: &quot;I&#x27;ll review repair 5 against the working tree and the 47-row probe, and check the grid, the `ic-&gt;arg[]` claim, the records, and 