note *** MY OWN BRIEF'S PREMISE WAS THAT `gdromcondlies` HELD THE LAST LIVE GUEST-REACHABLE HOST KILLS.  IT IS FALSE, AND THE FIRST FILE I SAMPLED REFUTED IT. ***  I stated it AS A QUESTION in that brief (*'have I confused "the queue knows of no others" with "there are no others"?'*), which is the only reason this was cheap to find -- and I found it myself, before the panel answered.  **THE CENSUS SAID WHERE TO LOOK AND WAS RIGHT.**  `exit_census.py` reports 99 live terminating calls inside `DEVICE_ACCESS` across 30 files; `dev_sgi_re.c` carries **21**, seven times the gdrom file.  It is the top of that list, and I sampled it for exactly that reason.  *** WHAT IS THERE, AND IT IS A CLASS THIS PROJECT HAS ALREADY FIXED ELSEWHERE: ***  the guard at the head of the CRIME_RE_TLB_A arm is  `if (len != 8) { fatal("TODO: unimplemented len=%i ..."); exit(1); }`  -- **a GUEST CHOOSING AN ACCESS WIDTH ends the host process.**  That is the `#337` class verbatim, whose own comment in `dev_wdc.c` reads *'a 3- or 8-byte access to the data port used to call exit(1) -- a GUEST choosing an access width killed the host process'*.  The adjacent arm kills on a plain READ (`fatal("TODO: read from CRIME_RE_TLB_A"); exit(1);`), which is the direction/offset class.  **REACHABILITY CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED**: `machine_sgi.c:500` calls `dev_sgi_re_init(machine, mem, 0x15000000)` and the device registers at `baseaddr + 0x1000` through `memory_device_register`.  It is a real device on a real machine, mapped into the guest address space.  **HONEST BOUND ON THE NUMBER, because this project keeps getting counts wrong: 21 is how many live terminating calls sit inside that file's `DEVICE_ACCESS` handlers.**  It is NOT a claim that 21 are individually reachable -- some may be guarded, and `dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c:1055` is the standing proof that a `DEVICE_ACCESS` site can be unreachable and take a hand-derived warrant to establish it.  What IS established: at least two of them are reachable by construction, and they are of classes already recognised as defects here.  *** THE GENERAL LESSON, AND IT IS ABOUT THE QUEUE RATHER THAN THIS DEVICE: A QUEUE-COMPLETE CLAIM IS NOT A TREE-COMPLETE ONE. ***  The adjudi

