  "_TENSE": "*** `state` IS PRESENT-TENSE; `closure.note` IS PAST-TENSE. *** The note is an EVENT LOG of what happened to a STAGE ('CLOSE (assess)' closes the assess stage). `state` asserts what the ROW still owes. **They are independent BY DESIGN** -- 23 rows share the string `CLOSE (assess)` across three states, and that is the ledger working correctly, not a defect: rows that experienced the same stage event legitimately differ in what else they owe. NEITHER can be derived from the other, and both attempts to do so have been measured wrong.",
  "closed": "Nothing outstanding; the claim was discharged BY WORK. Mechanical companions, era-scoped: commits, closure.by, and witness if closed on/after 2026-08-19.",
  "dropped": "Nothing outstanding; the claim was retired WITHOUT work, with the reason. Confusing this with `closed` is the es438 class -- both mean 'nothing owed', and misstating WHY is what misleads a future reader.",
