codex
An in-memory conversion leaves all nine closed rows with live review holds, plus a research hold on `sgirekills`. None has a later genuine answer that clears its final wall. The census also exposes an omitted October 16 failure; unlike the final walls, that older failure has later dated answers. The remaining distinction is policy: correcting a false state is already authorized by the ledger’s rules, while allowing closure with pending review would need an explicit exception.

